1
00:02:17,526 --> 00:02:18,845
My Halime.

2
00:02:19,886 --> 00:02:21,605
Halime.

3
00:02:25,606 --> 00:02:27,125
No.

4
00:02:29,206 --> 00:02:32,725
This is just another game. I don't believe you.

5
00:02:33,686 --> 00:02:35,085
I don't believe you!

6
00:02:35,246 --> 00:02:37,005
What game are you up to?

7
00:02:37,206 --> 00:02:39,765
This isn't a game, Osman.

8
00:02:40,846 --> 00:02:43,845
This is as real as your Bala
who you thought was dead.

9
00:02:45,006 --> 00:02:46,885
And for this moment,

10
00:02:48,526 --> 00:02:50,165
...I have waited too long.

11
00:02:51,966 --> 00:02:54,125
My vengeance is completed.

12
00:02:55,726 --> 00:02:57,485
Everything is over.

13
00:03:32,926 --> 00:03:35,325
Today, you're going to die.

14
00:03:37,406 --> 00:03:39,885
My Halime, is that you?

15
00:04:17,326 --> 00:04:19,084
Halime..

16
00:04:53,686 --> 00:04:57,645
-Meryem.
-My name is...

17
00:05:02,926 --> 00:05:05,285
..Poena.

18
00:05:12,526 --> 00:05:14,605
I've brought your daughter.

19
00:05:15,046 --> 00:05:16,765
...Osman Bey.

20
00:05:22,886 --> 00:05:25,085
Halime.

21
00:05:36,006 --> 00:05:37,685
My daughter.

22
00:05:53,766 --> 00:05:55,925
Damn it, Poena.

23
00:05:57,566 --> 00:05:59,845
Damn it! What's going on with you?

24
00:06:07,766 --> 00:06:10,205
What game are you up to again?

25
00:06:11,966 --> 00:06:13,845
What game?

26
00:06:15,086 --> 00:06:16,965
I don't believe you.

27
00:06:18,646 --> 00:06:19,925
I don't believe you.

28
00:06:20,126 --> 00:06:22,045
You have to believe, Osman.

29
00:06:23,006 --> 00:06:25,845
I've been waiting for this moment for years.

30
00:06:26,926 --> 00:06:29,165
I didn't plan this in one day.

31
00:06:29,886 --> 00:06:33,085
I thought about every detail patiently.

32
00:06:35,086 --> 00:06:40,005
I took away your daughter from you, Osman.

33
00:06:44,886 --> 00:06:47,045
Halime, is that you?

34
00:06:47,806 --> 00:06:50,725
Is that you, my Halime?

35
00:06:51,886 --> 00:06:53,165
My baby.

36
00:06:56,126 --> 00:07:02,125
-Halime, is that you?
-Look at me.

37
00:07:02,766 --> 00:07:07,205
If you hurt my Halime

38
00:07:07,686 --> 00:07:13,125
If this is true, I will kill you.

39
00:07:14,206 --> 00:07:20,045
I raised your daughter as a true Christian...

40
00:07:20,886 --> 00:07:24,365
...who was hostile against you and your country.

41
00:07:28,406 --> 00:07:32,605
Ask Bala if you don't believe
me. She saw her talisman.

42
00:07:37,966 --> 00:07:40,125
She's right, Osman.

43
00:07:40,926 --> 00:07:43,925
I had written the prayer in it myself.

44
00:07:44,726 --> 00:07:46,405
She's right.

45
00:07:49,806 --> 00:07:51,485
Bala, is that true?

46
00:07:52,086 --> 00:07:53,845
It's Halime.

47
00:07:54,686 --> 00:07:56,445
Her talisman.

48
00:08:03,966 --> 00:08:06,565
How can I make you believe, Osman?

49
00:08:09,086 --> 00:08:10,565
Shall I..

50
00:08:12,166 --> 00:08:14,765
...tell you your daughter's favorite fairy tale?

51
00:08:16,406 --> 00:08:21,165
The wolf and the baby gazelle.

52
00:08:30,646 --> 00:08:33,125
How do you know that?

53
00:08:33,765 --> 00:08:35,765
How do you know?

54
00:08:36,206 --> 00:08:38,565
Your daughter told me, Osman.

55
00:08:39,726 --> 00:08:41,683
If you hurt her.

56
00:08:42,166 --> 00:08:46,405
If you hurt her, I will cut your throat!

57
00:08:46,726 --> 00:08:48,165
Look, Bala.

58
00:08:49,766 --> 00:08:51,845
Osman believes too.

59
00:09:00,806 --> 00:09:02,165
But it's over.

60
00:09:03,566 --> 00:09:07,205
I will never let you two get her back.

61
00:09:08,686 --> 00:09:11,165
All of you are going to die.

62
00:09:31,446 --> 00:09:36,285
Today everything is going to happen as I want.

63
00:09:37,246 --> 00:09:41,125
I won't kill you once but a thousand times.

64
00:09:49,646 --> 00:09:51,325
Bala.

65
00:09:53,926 --> 00:09:56,325
Say goodbye to your daughter.

66
00:10:32,646 --> 00:10:33,725
Halime.

67
00:10:35,646 --> 00:10:39,205
Halime!

68
00:10:55,606 --> 00:10:57,965
The temple's defense has been broken.

69
00:10:58,886 --> 00:11:00,845
I was right about my doubts again.

70
00:11:02,686 --> 00:11:05,965
Osman has entered his
grave, waiting for his death.

71
00:11:06,966 --> 00:11:13,565
In this temple, his heart will crack
from the pain and will be laid at my feet.

72
00:11:39,206 --> 00:11:42,805
Damn it. Damn it! What is happening to you?

73
00:12:08,726 --> 00:12:10,325
Damn it, it was over.

74
00:12:12,806 --> 00:12:16,005
It was going to be over today!

75
00:12:16,126 --> 00:12:21,605
No one can save you from my
hands. You will beg me to die!

76
00:12:21,806 --> 00:12:24,445
We will see who will beg, Osman!

77
00:12:26,286 --> 00:12:27,925
I will kill you!

78
00:12:38,006 --> 00:12:41,525
-Kill them all! -Halime!

79
00:12:46,086 --> 00:12:50,165
Today, not even your corpse will leave here.

80
00:13:34,526 --> 00:13:38,845
Come on brothers! Come on!

81
00:13:55,726 --> 00:13:58,285
You cannot kill me Osman.

82
00:13:58,326 --> 00:14:00,965
I am the only one who
knows where your daughter is.

83
00:14:07,886 --> 00:14:09,965
If you kill me...

84
00:14:12,366 --> 00:14:13,485
...you will...

85
00:14:14,806 --> 00:14:17,365
...never find your daughter.

86
00:14:21,886 --> 00:14:23,085
Never.

87
00:14:26,126 --> 00:14:28,045
You will die!

88
00:14:35,686 --> 00:14:36,725
Halime!

89
00:14:37,806 --> 00:14:41,245
Halime, my daughter! -Bala!

90
00:14:41,846 --> 00:14:45,005
Osman... -Is it Halime?

91
00:14:46,766 --> 00:14:49,605
The burn mark. The burn mark, Osman.

92
00:14:50,446 --> 00:14:54,925
Let me see... No! -No...

93
00:14:55,286 --> 00:14:57,885
No, it's not Halime! It's not...

94
00:14:58,726 --> 00:15:01,205
-Snake...
It's not her.

95
00:15:01,286 --> 00:15:04,405
No, my Halime is alive. My Halime is alive.

96
00:15:05,486 --> 00:15:06,525
Snake..

97
00:15:07,606 --> 00:15:08,405
Where is she?

98
00:15:08,406 --> 00:15:11,925
Where is Halime? Where is she?
-My Bey! My Bey!

99
00:15:12,046 --> 00:15:15,325
Ulugan is coming here. There
are many of them, my Bey.

100
00:15:16,766 --> 00:15:21,285
Mother... Mother! -My son

101
00:15:21,686 --> 00:15:23,565
Thanks to You, my Allah.

102
00:15:24,406 --> 00:15:27,525
-You are alive, mother. -I am.

103
00:15:29,526 --> 00:15:31,525
Orhan.

104
00:15:31,526 --> 00:15:32,645
Thanks to Allah...

105
00:15:32,646 --> 00:15:34,165
I am alright, my son. -You are.

106
00:15:34,166 --> 00:15:35,805
I am alright, thanks to Allah.

107
00:15:38,406 --> 00:15:40,085
Are we going to fight, my Bey?

108
00:15:40,406 --> 00:15:43,165
It doesn't even have a door to defend, brother.

109
00:15:43,246 --> 00:15:44,805
How are we going to fight?

110
00:15:47,806 --> 00:15:50,405
I will shield myself and hold the door, my Bey.

111
00:15:51,126 --> 00:15:52,165
My Bey...

112
00:15:52,246 --> 00:15:54,125
We don't have enough equipment.

113
00:15:54,206 --> 00:15:58,525
There is a chance we won't let them
through, but we will suffer heavy losses.

114
00:15:58,886 --> 00:16:03,205
My brother is right, father.
What are we going to do now? -Today...

115
00:16:03,406 --> 00:16:06,765
...we cannot fight with Ulugan. Come on.

116
00:16:07,086 --> 00:16:08,565
We'll go this way.

117
00:16:11,446 --> 00:16:12,485
Come on, mother.

118
00:16:48,886 --> 00:16:50,965
There are only the dead here, Ulugan.

119
00:16:52,646 --> 00:16:54,525
Osman saved Bala.

120
00:16:56,006 --> 00:16:58,605
Sofia told us that this place was safe.

121
00:16:58,926 --> 00:17:01,485
That witch fell victim to her own arrogance.

122
00:17:05,846 --> 00:17:07,165
Osman..

123
00:17:08,486 --> 00:17:11,723
...must have saved his Hatun, since he ran away.

124
00:17:13,964 --> 00:17:17,085
But their joy will come together with sorrow.

125
00:17:35,606 --> 00:17:36,645
Blood..

126
00:17:39,206 --> 00:17:41,045
My lungs are filled with blood.

127
00:17:42,806 --> 00:17:43,965
They are close.

128
00:17:45,246 --> 00:17:46,645
We will find them.

129
00:17:48,606 --> 00:17:54,325
They will have died before the
blood on their swords gets dry.

130
00:18:05,926 --> 00:18:09,765
Damn it... Damn it... It was going to be over!

131
00:18:12,766 --> 00:18:19,525
They ran away again!

132
00:18:23,806 --> 00:18:25,045
Come closer..

133
00:18:39,086 --> 00:18:40,125
Poena!

134
00:18:43,366 --> 00:18:44,445
Hristo!

135
00:19:01,006 --> 00:19:02,365
Why Poena?

136
00:19:02,886 --> 00:19:04,805
Tell me, why?

137
00:19:05,326 --> 00:19:07,165
Why didn't you attack them?

138
00:19:07,846 --> 00:19:11,445
It was going to be over, you
were going to take your revenge!

139
00:19:11,886 --> 00:19:12,925
Why?!

140
00:19:14,406 --> 00:19:15,485
I was afraid.

141
00:19:17,846 --> 00:19:19,205
Afraid?

142
00:19:24,086 --> 00:19:26,085
Lift your head, Poena.

143
00:19:28,966 --> 00:19:32,725
You were raised to take revenge for your family.

144
00:19:33,686 --> 00:19:35,885
I raised you!

145
00:19:36,366 --> 00:19:37,405
I did!

146
00:19:38,326 --> 00:19:41,125
Why were you afraid Poena? How?!

147
00:19:43,246 --> 00:19:44,285
Revenge...

148
00:19:45,246 --> 00:19:47,805
...is the only thing that keeps me strong.

149
00:19:48,326 --> 00:19:51,245
I was afraid for a moment.

150
00:19:52,166 --> 00:19:53,205
That's all.

151
00:20:05,086 --> 00:20:07,205
I swear to God

152
00:20:08,766 --> 00:20:11,365
...it won't happen again, aunt.

153
00:20:15,246 --> 00:20:17,285
I know it won't, my little bird.

154
00:20:21,126 --> 00:20:22,285
I will do...

155
00:20:23,766 --> 00:20:25,605
..everything I can to fix this.

156
00:20:26,446 --> 00:20:28,605
I will do whatever you ask of me, aunt.

157
00:20:29,166 --> 00:20:30,285
Look Poena.

158
00:20:31,606 --> 00:20:32,725
Turks..

159
00:20:34,006 --> 00:20:37,365
...even in moments of joy,
carry doubts within themselves.

160
00:20:38,246 --> 00:20:43,565
That's why you'll go back to
them and wait for my order.

161
00:20:44,246 --> 00:20:46,605
Don't draw suspicion onto yourself.

162
00:20:47,206 --> 00:20:48,445
What's on your mind?

163
00:20:49,166 --> 00:20:53,165
I have planted such poison in
Osman and Bala's minds that...

164
00:20:55,126 --> 00:20:59,125
...they will walk to their deaths on their own.

165
00:21:13,326 --> 00:21:14,765
Let's have some rest.

166
00:21:15,046 --> 00:21:16,365
Mother... -Children.

167
00:21:16,366 --> 00:21:18,045
Thanks to Allah, you are alive.

168
00:21:18,246 --> 00:21:19,445
Thanks to Allah.

169
00:21:19,446 --> 00:21:21,525
Thanks to Allah. -Uluga

170
00:21:21,686 --> 00:21:23,445
...must be chasing us now.

171
00:21:23,486 --> 00:21:26,765
Let's have some rest first,
then we will leave the forest.

172
00:21:27,166 --> 00:21:29,725
-Stay on alert. 
-Okay my Bey.

173
00:21:32,766 --> 00:21:33,805
My Bey.

174
00:21:34,966 --> 00:21:37,045
Your wound is still bleeding, Osman.

175
00:21:37,726 --> 00:21:40,245
We cannot let it bleed.
We have to burn the wound.

176
00:21:44,126 --> 00:21:50,005
Bala, you've treated many of my
wounds. Don't worry. This wound will heal.

177
00:21:52,486 --> 00:21:56,845
But the wound in my heart does not heal, Osman.

178
00:21:57,286 --> 00:22:00,378
We need to find our
Halime, our daughter.

179
00:22:00,390 --> 00:22:04,085
We will find Halime and
take Sofia, don't worry.

180
00:22:15,446 --> 00:22:16,485
Osman!

181
00:22:19,166 --> 00:22:22,405
I was looking for you. Soon...

182
00:22:23,086 --> 00:22:26,165
...the souls of these trees
will be watered with your blood.

183
00:22:29,046 --> 00:22:33,125
-My Bey, they are coming in large numbers.
-They are approaching, father.

184
00:22:33,126 --> 00:22:35,605
We will split our forces
in two. Orhan, Alaeddin...

185
00:22:35,606 --> 00:22:37,445
...you will go to the southern side.

186
00:22:37,446 --> 00:22:39,245
Bala and the others will come with me.

187
00:22:39,246 --> 00:22:42,543
After getting rid of them, we
will meet at the secret tribe.

188
00:22:42,555 --> 00:22:43,965
Yes my Bey. Come on Alps.

189
00:22:44,086 --> 00:22:45,125
Come on.

190
00:22:51,566 --> 00:22:55,325
Come on.

191
00:23:02,766 --> 00:23:04,165
They split in two.

192
00:23:04,446 --> 00:23:06,045
Which way will we go, Ulugan?

193
00:23:06,046 --> 00:23:07,525
Osman is my prey.

194
00:23:07,806 --> 00:23:09,645
You go after his little dogs.

195
00:23:15,286 --> 00:23:17,605
Osman Bey's Secret Tents

196
00:23:37,296 --> 00:23:41,485
Ulgen, tell them to grind one more sack
of wheat, so we will have enough, alright?

197
00:23:41,486 --> 00:23:43,165
I will tell the Alps now.

198
00:23:46,046 --> 00:23:50,725
After all this pain, it feels like the
tribe has finally found some peace, right?

199
00:23:50,886 --> 00:23:51,925
Right.

200
00:23:52,446 --> 00:23:53,885
Sure they did.

201
00:23:54,766 --> 00:23:58,085
It's the joy and excitement
of the sacred Ramadan.

202
00:24:02,406 --> 00:24:05,845
Now we will only wait for my
father and the others to return.

203
00:24:05,846 --> 00:24:08,365
Tonight, we will have our first suhoor.

204
00:24:13,526 --> 00:24:18,925
My Bala mother would want the
same meal to be served in every tent.

205
00:24:29,686 --> 00:24:30,765
Fatma..

206
00:24:35,926 --> 00:24:38,725
...we will do the same,
my beautiful eyed sister.

207
00:24:39,086 --> 00:24:42,885
We will continue from where
my mother left off, right Fatma?

208
00:24:44,646 --> 00:24:49,205
We will all protect her
trust together, God willing.

209
00:24:51,406 --> 00:24:53,285
Right, sisters?

210
00:24:53,286 --> 00:24:54,805
God willing.

211
00:24:55,966 --> 00:24:57,005
God willing.

212
00:25:14,326 --> 00:25:15,845
Osman!

213
00:25:16,366 --> 00:25:18,765
You can't run away this time!

214
00:25:20,446 --> 00:25:22,565
Osman, they're coming closer.

215
00:25:22,926 --> 00:25:24,925
We'll handle this with our minds.

216
00:25:25,206 --> 00:25:28,965
Swords won't get out of
sheathes even for vengeance.

217
00:25:29,526 --> 00:25:31,005
Let them come.

218
00:25:36,806 --> 00:25:38,525
They're getting faster.

219
00:25:39,406 --> 00:25:43,365
The spirits of the ground
and the sky are with us, Altuga.

220
00:25:44,166 --> 00:25:46,605
Osman's kin will vanish today.

221
00:25:52,606 --> 00:25:53,965
They're still coming.

222
00:25:54,126 --> 00:25:56,925
-What's your plan, Osman?
-Let them come.

223
00:25:57,166 --> 00:26:00,925
The moment they think they'll
catch us, we will get rid of them.

224
00:26:01,766 --> 00:26:03,285
Come on.

225
00:26:10,726 --> 00:26:13,925
Faster. We won't let them leave this forest.

226
00:26:29,166 --> 00:26:31,965
-We got rid of them, my Bey.
-No, not yet.

227
00:26:32,046 --> 00:26:33,725
But we will.

228
00:26:34,486 --> 00:26:39,325
-Shoot the birds on the tree in the north.
-Alright, my Bey.

229
00:26:45,806 --> 00:26:47,685
Ya Allah!

230
00:26:52,646 --> 00:26:56,005
They're going to the
north. Birds are flying off.

231
00:26:57,526 --> 00:26:59,685
Let's go to the north.

232
00:27:01,446 --> 00:27:03,085
Let's go.

233
00:27:22,166 --> 00:27:25,525
You're going to the north now.

234
00:27:32,606 --> 00:27:36,045
-We almost reached the horses. Come on.
-They're getting closer.

235
00:27:36,126 --> 00:27:38,325
What now, my Shahzade?

236
00:27:40,606 --> 00:27:44,125
We'll show those jackals who
the prey and the predator are.

237
00:27:44,526 --> 00:27:47,565
I know what's in your mind, my Shahzade.

238
00:27:48,006 --> 00:27:50,965
The game with wolves ends with blood.

239
00:27:51,406 --> 00:27:56,125
At the entrance of the pass, we'll
have a welcome party for them.

240
00:27:56,486 --> 00:28:00,485
-Alps, take positions on both sides.
-Alps, grab your bows.

241
00:28:05,766 --> 00:28:07,405
Keep coming.

242
00:28:11,686 --> 00:28:13,125
Ilbay!

243
00:28:16,046 --> 00:28:19,005
Are you looking for us, you dog?

244
00:28:20,726 --> 00:28:23,005
Alaaddin and the others aren't here.

245
00:28:23,166 --> 00:28:26,005
They split up.
-You...

246
00:28:26,886 --> 00:28:31,925
You are a poor dog whose leash
Mongolians are holding, Ilbay!

247
00:28:33,086 --> 00:28:36,445
Who are you to even kill us?

248
00:28:37,246 --> 00:28:39,445
I will skin you, Orhan!

249
00:28:39,846 --> 00:28:42,365
Keep walking to your death.

250
00:28:42,846 --> 00:28:45,565
-Attack!
-Keep coming.

251
00:28:48,246 --> 00:28:50,205
Begum, watch out!

252
00:28:53,566 --> 00:28:55,405
Praise be.

253
00:28:56,686 --> 00:28:58,405
I will skin you, Orhan!

254
00:28:58,766 --> 00:29:00,725
Just be patient!

255
00:29:02,566 --> 00:29:05,925
With this trick, we'll get rid of those fools.

256
00:29:06,086 --> 00:29:09,045
My father must have got rid of Ulugan too.

257
00:29:15,166 --> 00:29:18,005
You jackals... Whoever challenges the lion...

258
00:29:18,126 --> 00:29:20,085
...will be the prey always.

259
00:29:20,246 --> 00:29:22,725
Let's go to the tribe now.

260
00:29:25,366 --> 00:29:27,885
I will make your drown in your blood, Orhan.

261
00:29:28,126 --> 00:29:29,885
You'll drown in your own blood!

262
00:29:44,366 --> 00:29:48,605
I was going to take revenge
from Osman and Bala today.

263
00:29:51,246 --> 00:29:52,805
Look.

264
00:29:54,206 --> 00:29:57,165
There isn't their blood on my hands.

265
00:30:02,206 --> 00:30:07,445
I'll hang all the guards in
the yard to make an example!

266
00:30:07,806 --> 00:30:09,725
Gather all of them.

267
00:30:10,606 --> 00:30:12,045
Fools!

268
00:30:12,446 --> 00:30:14,805
They shouldn't have let them!

269
00:30:15,806 --> 00:30:17,645
Yes, my lady.

270
00:30:18,446 --> 00:30:20,045
Fortunately,

271
00:30:21,206 --> 00:30:23,085
...I poisoned Bala.

272
00:30:24,086 --> 00:30:27,485
They'll fall in my clutches for their Halime.

273
00:30:28,086 --> 00:30:32,845
My lady, Ulugan will hold you
responsible for Osman's escape.

274
00:30:33,206 --> 00:30:36,485
What should we do if he comes to the fortress?

275
00:30:37,646 --> 00:30:39,325
Ulugan.

276
00:30:40,486 --> 00:30:43,845
Ulugan can't take the
risk of losing the alliance.

277
00:30:44,166 --> 00:30:46,365
He's aware of my power.

278
00:30:47,246 --> 00:30:52,685
He already knows turning against each other
instead of destroying Osman would be stupid.

279
00:30:54,566 --> 00:30:58,085
When I punish the idiot guards,

280
00:31:00,766 --> 00:31:03,205
...he will cool down.

281
00:31:04,886 --> 00:31:06,725
Then we will..

282
00:31:09,566 --> 00:31:11,445
...turn the frontiers...

283
00:31:14,566 --> 00:31:17,925
...into hell for Osman together.

284
00:31:20,686 --> 00:31:24,085
Osman Bey's coming!
Osman Bey's coming!

285
00:31:57,926 --> 00:32:00,685
-Mother?
-Mother...

286
00:32:02,846 --> 00:32:04,525
Mother.

287
00:32:08,006 --> 00:32:11,325
Is... Is this a dream?

288
00:32:12,006 --> 00:32:14,125
For real?

289
00:32:15,086 --> 00:32:17,005
She's alive!

290
00:32:17,206 --> 00:32:19,965
-Mother?
-Is this for real?

291
00:32:20,046 --> 00:32:23,805
-She's really back!
-Mother!

292
00:32:30,486 --> 00:32:32,685
Mother!

293
00:32:33,406 --> 00:32:36,725
Mother! I was so scared!

294
00:32:37,526 --> 00:32:41,845
-Mother.
-I thought we lost you.

295
00:32:42,046 --> 00:32:44,245
This is really you.

296
00:32:53,526 --> 00:32:55,805
-My Fatma.
-Mother.

297
00:32:56,446 --> 00:32:59,405
I haven't gone anywhere, Fatma. I'm here.

298
00:32:59,686 --> 00:33:02,005
This is really you, mother.

299
00:33:02,366 --> 00:33:05,845
How did that happen, mother? Alaaddin!

300
00:33:07,366 --> 00:33:10,165
Orhan, is this a dream?

301
00:33:10,166 --> 00:33:11,765
It's for real, Holofira.

302
00:33:12,006 --> 00:33:13,845
Yet it was a nightmare before.

303
00:33:19,606 --> 00:33:23,005
I don't get it. How did that happen?

304
00:33:23,446 --> 00:33:26,045
Mother, how could you survive?

305
00:33:26,446 --> 00:33:27,845
It was Sofia's game.

306
00:33:27,886 --> 00:33:30,485
She saved me from the fire and imprisoned me.

307
00:33:30,526 --> 00:33:32,925
And Osman Bey saved me from her.

308
00:33:40,606 --> 00:33:44,085
-Father.
My Fatma.

309
00:33:48,446 --> 00:33:52,365
As this is you... Who was
the one who got burned?

310
00:33:53,646 --> 00:33:55,885
What kind of game is this, father?

311
00:33:56,806 --> 00:33:59,485
-Mother...
-My dear.

312
00:34:02,686 --> 00:34:04,685
Praise be, Praise be.

313
00:34:05,366 --> 00:34:07,765
Come on, hatuns.

314
00:34:08,286 --> 00:34:10,925
Bala is exhausted. She should get some rest.

315
00:34:11,606 --> 00:34:13,965
Right, Bala? You should rest.

316
00:34:14,045 --> 00:34:16,005
Fatma, come here.

317
00:34:16,045 --> 00:34:19,085
I'm fine but we need to
cauterize your wound, my Bey.

318
00:34:19,166 --> 00:34:22,245
-Alaaddin, check it out. -No. No need for that.

319
00:34:22,246 --> 00:34:25,485
My wound has recovered.

320
00:34:30,406 --> 00:34:34,005
My father was suspecting
that mother might be alive.

321
00:34:34,166 --> 00:34:37,324
But he didn't want to tell
us before he was sure.

322
00:34:38,206 --> 00:34:40,485
Meryem brought the good news.

323
00:34:40,686 --> 00:34:43,324
Without her, we couldn't
have heard the soldiers.

324
00:34:43,366 --> 00:34:45,885
And we might be still looking for Bala.

325
00:34:46,485 --> 00:34:48,485
Was Meryem with you?

326
00:34:48,525 --> 00:34:50,804
We got worried about her.

327
00:34:51,326 --> 00:34:54,525
We sent Meryem back to
the tribe. Didn't she come?

328
00:34:54,886 --> 00:34:56,245
She didn't.

329
00:34:58,966 --> 00:35:01,845
May Allah protect her. She
may have got into trouble?

330
00:35:05,246 --> 00:35:06,965
-Boran.
-My Bey.

331
00:35:06,966 --> 00:35:10,485
Send alps to search everywhere up to Akhisar.

332
00:35:10,766 --> 00:35:12,485
As you order, my Bey.

333
00:35:13,046 --> 00:35:15,125
Bala, you should rest.

334
00:35:15,486 --> 00:35:17,325
Inform the Beys.

335
00:35:19,046 --> 00:35:20,965
We will have a council.

336
00:35:37,126 --> 00:35:39,645
Where is their damn hidden tribe?

337
00:35:42,606 --> 00:35:44,525
Osman's alps...

338
00:35:45,446 --> 00:35:47,765
...left me somewhere around here.

339
00:35:48,686 --> 00:35:53,205
The tribe should be nearby. But where?

340
00:36:02,326 --> 00:36:06,045
Osman Bey Secret Tents

341
00:36:10,686 --> 00:36:12,925
They think...

342
00:36:13,606 --> 00:36:16,685
...I've fallen weak without a land.

343
00:36:17,766 --> 00:36:21,925
But as long as we have
the fire of faith in our hearts.

344
00:36:22,446 --> 00:36:24,925
...as long as we have hope.

345
00:36:29,006 --> 00:36:30,925
..we will..

346
00:36:31,966 --> 00:36:34,845
...we will never give up.

347
00:36:38,766 --> 00:36:40,445
Well..

348
00:36:41,126 --> 00:36:46,245
If we were to make a move
against Ulugan to take our tribe back

349
00:36:48,126 --> 00:36:50,805
...we would be outnumbered.

350
00:36:51,086 --> 00:36:58,085
Then we should save all the Turkmen Beys like
Sahin Bey living in captivity from Mongolians.

351
00:36:58,406 --> 00:37:02,565
No. It's the first move
Ulugan would predict.

352
00:37:06,806 --> 00:37:08,645
We will..

353
00:37:09,046 --> 00:37:12,965
...take the power on our side
as Ulugan could never imagine.

354
00:37:15,006 --> 00:37:16,285
The power...

355
00:37:16,806 --> 00:37:19,565
...is the leaderless Turkmen...

356
00:37:20,886 --> 00:37:23,005
...beyond our borders.

357
00:37:31,246 --> 00:37:33,685
I see the concern in your eyes.

358
00:37:34,526 --> 00:37:36,965
Tell me what you think.

359
00:37:37,886 --> 00:37:39,525
My Bey.

360
00:37:39,806 --> 00:37:43,325
They are rebellious Turkmen
who never take orders.

361
00:37:44,206 --> 00:37:46,925
So I don't know how we can...

362
00:37:47,366 --> 00:37:50,245
...make them join our fight.

363
00:37:52,566 --> 00:37:54,525
Cerkutay Bey.

364
00:37:54,926 --> 00:37:56,485
Yusuf Bey.

365
00:37:58,046 --> 00:38:01,325
Do you agree Boran Bey on this?

366
00:38:12,246 --> 00:38:16,605
My sons, tell me what you think.

367
00:38:20,846 --> 00:38:24,965
It's hard to get support
from the rebellious Turkmen.

368
00:38:25,366 --> 00:38:29,485
Yet our Bey has always taught us...

369
00:38:29,526 --> 00:38:32,645
There is always a way for those who want to walk

370
00:38:32,646 --> 00:38:36,285
...a lock for those who want to break
and a door for those who want to open.

371
00:38:36,286 --> 00:38:38,485
Allah knows best.

372
00:38:40,966 --> 00:38:42,005
Allah knows best.

373
00:38:42,046 --> 00:38:46,045
-Do I have permission, my Bey?
-Come in, Kanyumaz.

374
00:38:49,086 --> 00:38:51,925
My Bey, I got important news.

375
00:38:52,046 --> 00:38:56,245
Ulugan demanded a great number of
nokers from beyond the borders, my Bey.

376
00:38:56,286 --> 00:39:01,085
-Yes?
-We have just broken their force.

377
00:39:02,606 --> 00:39:05,925
We can't let them regain strength, my Bey.

378
00:39:06,566 --> 00:39:09,245
We can't but how?

379
00:39:10,126 --> 00:39:12,725
There is definitely a way.

380
00:39:13,326 --> 00:39:15,365
Definitely.

381
00:39:17,646 --> 00:39:22,525
The stone we throw should
both help us get stronger...

382
00:39:23,246 --> 00:39:27,725
...and break Ulugan' wings and legs.

383
00:39:31,046 --> 00:39:36,005
Rebellious Turkmen beyond our borders...

384
00:39:38,606 --> 00:39:40,085
Kanyumaz.
-My Bey.

385
00:39:40,206 --> 00:39:43,005
-Send a message to them.
-As you order, my Bey.

386
00:39:46,166 --> 00:39:50,445
I will be waiting for them in Serinsu.

387
00:39:51,486 --> 00:39:52,805
But...

388
00:39:54,966 --> 00:39:57,365
Ayaz Bey...

389
00:39:59,606 --> 00:40:02,085
You will see Ayaz Bey personally, Boran.

390
00:40:02,406 --> 00:40:04,205
As you order, my Bey.

391
00:40:30,246 --> 00:40:32,525
Osman.

392
00:40:32,526 --> 00:40:34,405
I will be your Azrael, Osman.

393
00:40:35,526 --> 00:40:37,365
I will send you and your dogs...

394
00:40:37,846 --> 00:40:42,045
..to seven layers down, to Erlik Khan.

395
00:40:42,726 --> 00:40:44,565
Where is Osman, Altuga?

396
00:40:45,166 --> 00:40:46,845
He hasn't reached Sogut, Ulugan.

397
00:40:48,406 --> 00:40:51,645
Since he knows we will corner
him there, he keeps moving.

398
00:40:52,006 --> 00:40:54,045
We don't know where he has settled.

399
00:40:56,726 --> 00:40:58,045
We lost many men.

400
00:40:59,086 --> 00:41:02,245
As long as Osman is alive, we will keep losing.

401
00:41:02,966 --> 00:41:05,845
Support noker units must have set out.

402
00:41:07,006 --> 00:41:10,325
Osman doesn't have Alps,
but we have many nokers.

403
00:41:11,646 --> 00:41:12,925
You are right.

404
00:41:13,326 --> 00:41:16,925
We will corner Osman before
he heals his wounds and kill him.

405
00:41:16,926 --> 00:41:18,485
Shut up, Hatun!

406
00:41:19,126 --> 00:41:20,165
Shut up!

407
00:41:21,606 --> 00:41:26,045
Because of your stupidity, Osman is still alive.

408
00:41:28,126 --> 00:41:30,125
Don't think Osman will stop.

409
00:41:30,166 --> 00:41:33,645
Just as he drew Sahin Bey to his side...

410
00:41:33,846 --> 00:41:36,605
...he will make the other Beys side with him.

411
00:41:36,726 --> 00:41:41,285
Have the tribe Beys lost their
minds to join Osman's side?

412
00:41:41,926 --> 00:41:44,405
What did Osman give them except death, Ulugan?

413
00:41:50,526 --> 00:41:54,685
Whatever he gave you he will give them too.

414
00:41:57,086 --> 00:42:00,165
Weren't you deceived by his words in the past?

415
00:42:04,966 --> 00:42:08,045
A wolf changes its fur.

416
00:42:09,766 --> 00:42:11,445
But it never changes its habits.

417
00:42:13,086 --> 00:42:14,685
Osman will not stop.

418
00:42:15,726 --> 00:42:17,645
We will stop him.

419
00:42:19,126 --> 00:42:20,845
Ulugan is right, Begum Hatun.

420
00:42:23,886 --> 00:42:24,925
Ulugan...

421
00:42:28,686 --> 00:42:31,685
...all tribe Beys will be scared of you.

422
00:42:32,886 --> 00:42:37,805
They will not be able to make a decision
when they think about joining Osman's side.

423
00:42:37,806 --> 00:42:39,845
But I know their weak spot.

424
00:42:45,126 --> 00:42:47,525
What are you thinking about, Ilbay?

425
00:42:47,686 --> 00:42:49,605
Osman's treasure is in our hands.

426
00:42:50,686 --> 00:42:51,765
I say..

427
00:42:52,646 --> 00:42:54,365
...we rain gold on Beys.

428
00:42:54,966 --> 00:42:59,965
Let's pull them to our side
with both swords and gold.

429
00:43:11,686 --> 00:43:17,485
The time will come when I
will cover their gold with blood.

430
00:43:18,926 --> 00:43:20,965
Let it be as you say, Ilbay.

431
00:43:22,126 --> 00:43:25,365
Call the Beys. Give them the gold.

432
00:43:33,086 --> 00:43:34,445
My mother.

433
00:43:35,406 --> 00:43:36,445
Mother.

434
00:43:38,206 --> 00:43:40,405
Don't ever leave again, alright?

435
00:43:41,406 --> 00:43:45,245
When you left, the peace of our family was gone.

436
00:43:48,446 --> 00:43:52,165
When I saw my father,
my brothers, and my aunts...

437
00:43:52,806 --> 00:43:55,005
...I thought we would never smile again.

438
00:43:57,046 --> 00:43:58,605
My dear daughter.

439
00:43:59,446 --> 00:44:01,445
Look, it's all over now, huh?

440
00:44:01,926 --> 00:44:03,245
Let me see

441
00:44:04,486 --> 00:44:07,885
Don't shed those pearl tears anymore.

442
00:44:08,126 --> 00:44:10,285
I would sacrifice myself for you.

443
00:44:10,686 --> 00:44:13,045
It's over. It's over now.

444
00:44:13,126 --> 00:44:15,365
All the Turkmens cried and mourned.

445
00:44:16,366 --> 00:44:20,805
May Allah never make us experience
the two days we went through again.

446
00:44:26,286 --> 00:44:28,485
My Gonca! -Mother...

447
00:44:29,646 --> 00:44:33,323
Alaeddin sent an ointment.
Let's apply it to your wounds.

448
00:44:33,335 --> 00:44:34,565
Let's apply it.

449
00:44:40,206 --> 00:44:43,925
Who knows what that demon did to you?
-She is a demon.

450
00:44:44,326 --> 00:44:45,645
She is a vicious demon.

451
00:44:46,966 --> 00:44:48,005
Mother.

452
00:44:48,686 --> 00:44:50,485
You look very tired.

453
00:44:51,086 --> 00:44:53,965
Let's apply the ointment.
And you rest for a while.

454
00:44:57,566 --> 00:45:01,005
That demon caused a deep wound in my heart.

455
00:45:04,086 --> 00:45:05,525
Meryem is coming, mother.

456
00:45:13,366 --> 00:45:15,805
Come on. Come on.

457
00:45:21,366 --> 00:45:22,405
Meryem.

458
00:45:25,246 --> 00:45:26,325
Bala Hatun.

459
00:45:34,686 --> 00:45:35,885
Thanks to Allah!

460
00:45:36,966 --> 00:45:38,645
Thanks to Allah, you are alive!

461
00:45:41,046 --> 00:45:45,005
Thanks to you, my daughter. Osman
Bey told me about the things you did.

462
00:45:45,006 --> 00:45:47,565
But you... Are you alright? Were you hurt?

463
00:45:47,566 --> 00:45:49,045
Mongols attacked.

464
00:45:49,886 --> 00:45:52,365
Alps protected me, I ran away but...

465
00:45:52,486 --> 00:45:56,045
...I couldn't find you since I
didn't know where the tribe was.

466
00:45:56,126 --> 00:45:59,525
Don't be afraid. It's all
over now. You are here.

467
00:46:00,606 --> 00:46:01,645
Meryem.

468
00:46:02,406 --> 00:46:04,165
Your bag is in our tent.

469
00:46:04,166 --> 00:46:06,685
If you need anything,
you can take it from there.

470
00:46:06,686 --> 00:46:08,285
Thank you, Gonca Hatun.

471
00:46:08,926 --> 00:46:10,645
Can I go and rest a bit?

472
00:46:10,966 --> 00:46:11,565
Go.

473
00:46:21,806 --> 00:46:25,845
My beautiful daughter...

474
00:46:25,846 --> 00:46:28,405
Come. Come here.

475
00:46:33,206 --> 00:46:37,291
Since you missed your
mother so much, let me make

476
00:46:37,303 --> 00:46:41,645
you a nice meal with my own
hands, huh? We're hungry.

477
00:46:41,646 --> 00:46:44,363
Your hands are hurt. You are
still bleeding. Don't do it now, huh?

478
00:46:44,375 --> 00:46:45,285
Yes.

479
00:46:45,486 --> 00:46:48,245
Go rest, my Bala. We
will take care of everything.

480
00:46:48,246 --> 00:46:49,525
Yes, Bala mother.

481
00:46:49,846 --> 00:46:53,765
We have even made
preparations for our first suhoor.

482
00:46:53,886 --> 00:46:58,245
Mother, it's Holofira's first
suhoor, that's why she is so excited.

483
00:46:59,726 --> 00:47:01,085
Praise be.

484
00:47:01,286 --> 00:47:03,965
First suhoor, huh? And with your baby.

485
00:47:07,406 --> 00:47:10,725
Thanks to Allah Who let us see the Ramadan.

486
00:47:10,966 --> 00:47:13,205
-Thanks to Allah.
-Thanks to Allah.

487
00:47:14,006 --> 00:47:16,405
Let's go.
Let's prepare it. Come on.

488
00:47:39,006 --> 00:47:42,015
In the name of Allah, the merciful, 
the compassionate.

489
00:47:42,846 --> 00:47:43,885
Meryem.

490
00:47:46,886 --> 00:47:48,125
Welcome.

491
00:47:48,366 --> 00:47:50,285
Thank you Alaeddin Bey.

492
00:47:52,126 --> 00:47:53,165
Meryem...

493
00:47:54,966 --> 00:47:57,605
...you did us such a favour that...

494
00:47:58,526 --> 00:47:59,725
..from now on..

495
00:48:00,406 --> 00:48:03,005
...from now on, see me as a brother.

496
00:48:03,206 --> 00:48:04,925
Thank you Alaeddin Bey.

497
00:48:04,926 --> 00:48:07,405
No, thank you. Thank you.

498
00:48:08,806 --> 00:48:13,885
From now on, if you have a problem or
need something, come and tell me. Alright?

499
00:48:18,486 --> 00:48:19,845
What is that in your hand?

500
00:48:24,886 --> 00:48:28,965
As I was going to find my dagger, I
found this around the burning cabin.

501
00:48:29,846 --> 00:48:34,005
I was curious about what
it is, so I wanted to ask you.

502
00:48:43,566 --> 00:48:44,605
Good.

503
00:48:45,166 --> 00:48:46,485
I'll keep this.

504
00:48:47,046 --> 00:48:48,525
I'll go and see what it is.

505
00:49:08,326 --> 00:49:09,365
Bala..

506
00:49:11,206 --> 00:49:13,165
You are dressing my wounds

507
00:49:16,086 --> 00:49:17,645
But your wounds...

508
00:49:19,486 --> 00:49:20,565
Look at them...

509
00:49:20,566 --> 00:49:23,005
You haven't even applied the ointment yet.

510
00:49:23,006 --> 00:49:27,725
What have they done to these hands I
couldn't touch? How could they torture you?

511
00:49:28,606 --> 00:49:30,685
She hurt us so deeply that...

512
00:49:31,486 --> 00:49:33,125
...I cannot feel any other pain.

513
00:49:35,886 --> 00:49:37,725
All this pain will pass.

514
00:49:38,246 --> 00:49:39,845
Just like these wounds.

515
00:49:40,486 --> 00:49:41,685
Don't worry.

516
00:49:42,086 --> 00:49:45,365
All the pain in our hearts will disappear.

517
00:49:46,286 --> 00:49:48,085
Our daughter is alive, my Osman.

518
00:49:49,006 --> 00:49:50,845
But she is in that demon's hands.

519
00:49:51,846 --> 00:49:55,765
Who knows how she raised
our daughter all these years?

520
00:49:58,366 --> 00:50:00,205
I still cannot believe it.

521
00:50:01,446 --> 00:50:03,645
I still cannot believe it.

522
00:50:04,126 --> 00:50:05,445
How could this happen?

523
00:50:06,206 --> 00:50:10,445
How could that dastard do this? How could she...

524
00:50:12,046 --> 00:50:15,645
...do this to a little girl?

525
00:50:16,126 --> 00:50:18,405
How could she do this to my daughter?

526
00:50:20,246 --> 00:50:24,325
That devil has set such a painful,
such a terrifying game that...

527
00:50:24,486 --> 00:50:27,445
..she waited all those years just to hurt us.

528
00:50:30,526 --> 00:50:32,725
Knowing Halime is alive...

529
00:50:33,566 --> 00:50:36,765
...makes me happy and kills me at the same time.

530
00:50:37,126 --> 00:50:39,805
Without a mother, a father... All alone...

531
00:50:41,126 --> 00:50:42,685
How could this happen, Bala?

532
00:50:43,206 --> 00:50:46,085
Who knows what lies did that...

533
00:50:47,326 --> 00:50:49,925
...dastard dog tell her?

534
00:50:50,086 --> 00:50:52,925
What deep wounds has
she caused in her heart, huh?

535
00:50:55,286 --> 00:50:56,685
"She kept crying.

536
00:50:58,086 --> 00:51:01,405
She asked for her mother
and father", said that devil.

537
00:51:03,846 --> 00:51:08,805
When I imagine her like that...
-Shh, alright.

538
00:51:09,366 --> 00:51:10,405
Alright.

539
00:51:11,206 --> 00:51:13,565
Look, our daughter is alive.

540
00:51:15,246 --> 00:51:17,565
And I will find her and bring her to you.

541
00:51:18,126 --> 00:51:25,845
I will make her pay for every tear
that falls from your gazelle eyes.

542
00:51:33,446 --> 00:51:36,525
Osman, I did not tell our
children since I did not ask you.

543
00:51:36,566 --> 00:51:38,685
What are we going to do? Will we tell them?

544
00:51:38,686 --> 00:51:40,125
Sure we will.

545
00:51:40,366 --> 00:51:43,285
We will, so they will
not mourn for their sister.

546
00:51:44,166 --> 00:51:46,245
They will become hopeful again.

547
00:51:50,046 --> 00:51:51,245
Come on, rest here.

548
00:51:52,766 --> 00:51:54,925
Come on, rest your head here.

549
00:51:55,086 --> 00:51:59,365
Rest so that our hopes can grow too.

550
00:52:19,686 --> 00:52:23,045
This is all the loot we've
obtained from the last raid, my Bey.

551
00:52:25,286 --> 00:52:26,925
The hunt has been fruitful.

552
00:52:27,526 --> 00:52:33,205
You know that the one with the sharpest
sword takes the largest share of the loots.

553
00:52:33,366 --> 00:52:35,685
This is how it should be distributed.

554
00:52:36,406 --> 00:52:37,925
Can I come in, my Bey?

555
00:52:38,486 --> 00:52:39,525
Come in.

556
00:52:43,246 --> 00:52:44,285
Ayaz Bey.

557
00:52:44,926 --> 00:52:48,125
Boran Bey from Kayis is
here. He wants to talk to you.

558
00:52:54,046 --> 00:53:00,325
Osman Bey who lost his lands and
the state sent his most loyal man then.

559
00:53:02,046 --> 00:53:04,245
He will ask us to side with him.

560
00:53:05,406 --> 00:53:10,765
Siding with Osman Bey means
facing the Mongol threat, my Bey.

561
00:53:16,726 --> 00:53:18,285
Let Boran Bey in.

562
00:53:36,206 --> 00:53:37,925
Peace be upon you Ayaz Bey.

563
00:53:37,926 --> 00:53:40,685
Peace be upon you too, Boran Bey. Welcome.

564
00:53:41,206 --> 00:53:42,245
Thank you.

565
00:53:43,286 --> 00:53:45,365
I came here with my Osman Bey's order.

566
00:53:45,766 --> 00:53:52,325
Osman Bey wants to meet you and all
the Turkmen Beys tomorrow at Serinsu.

567
00:53:52,766 --> 00:53:54,805
What does Osman Bey want from us?

568
00:53:55,286 --> 00:53:56,685
I am just a messenger.

569
00:53:57,526 --> 00:54:01,085
You have to go there and hear
directly from my Bey what he has to say.

570
00:54:12,206 --> 00:54:14,165
Tell me Ayaz Bey

571
00:54:16,566 --> 00:54:19,125
Will you accept my Bey's invitation?

572
00:54:29,286 --> 00:54:32,085
My father loves soup made with bone broth.

573
00:54:32,286 --> 00:54:36,205
If we throw it into the pot now,
it will only be ready for suhoor.

574
00:54:41,406 --> 00:54:43,125
We cannot do this, Gonca.

575
00:54:43,686 --> 00:54:46,565
-We can't make it to suhoor.
-No.

576
00:54:48,446 --> 00:54:50,325
We need strength.

577
00:54:51,206 --> 00:54:55,525
We work here, but the Shahzades
are enjoying themselves by the fire.

578
00:55:03,366 --> 00:55:04,565
Alaeddin Bey.

579
00:55:07,646 --> 00:55:10,245
Alaeddin, brother...

580
00:55:10,606 --> 00:55:13,245
You are done, she called you a Bey.

581
00:55:13,566 --> 00:55:16,165
I heard, brother. I heard.

582
00:55:18,526 --> 00:55:19,565
But..

583
00:55:21,046 --> 00:55:22,085
..look.

584
00:55:23,046 --> 00:55:25,165
-Orhan Bey.
-Holofira Hatun.

585
00:55:26,606 --> 00:55:29,645
-I guess you are really tired.
-No.

586
00:55:38,726 --> 00:55:40,005
What happened my Hatun?

587
00:55:43,326 --> 00:55:44,805
Why did you call us?

588
00:55:46,766 --> 00:55:51,525
We go and join battles with you, right?
-Yes, so?

589
00:55:52,006 --> 00:55:53,045
So...

590
00:55:53,326 --> 00:55:57,645
..you will help us while we are cooking meals.

591
00:56:10,366 --> 00:56:11,405
How?

592
00:56:11,966 --> 00:56:14,765
Are we... are we going to prepare meals?

593
00:56:15,446 --> 00:56:17,965
My Gonca, don't... How
is that going to happen...

594
00:56:17,966 --> 00:56:19,725
It is going to happen. Like this.

595
00:56:23,166 --> 00:56:24,405
So...

596
00:56:25,806 --> 00:56:27,565
...this is how it works.

597
00:56:28,486 --> 00:56:33,205
You can make forty valiants
listen to you on the battlefield, but...

598
00:56:33,966 --> 00:56:36,925
...you can't make the
daughters of others listen to you.

599
00:56:36,926 --> 00:56:39,565
Fatma!

600
00:56:40,446 --> 00:56:41,485
Come on.

601
00:56:42,246 --> 00:56:45,165
Let's show how to prepare
and cook meals to them.

602
00:56:45,526 --> 00:56:48,125
-May it be easy.
-May it be easy.

603
00:56:48,126 --> 00:56:49,565
Let's show them, brother.

604
00:56:50,806 --> 00:56:55,405
Let's do so, but I swear
Alps will make fun of us.

605
00:56:57,166 --> 00:56:58,725
Brother.

606
00:56:59,166 --> 00:57:00,765
Nothing will happen.

607
00:57:01,126 --> 00:57:04,125
Didn't my father also cook for us in the past?

608
00:57:06,726 --> 00:57:11,725
And I remember the days
when you kneaded the dough.

609
00:57:11,726 --> 00:57:12,885
Sister..

610
00:57:15,606 --> 00:57:16,845
She is joking...

611
00:57:17,766 --> 00:57:18,805
Come on.

612
00:57:21,046 --> 00:57:23,485
-Ya Allah!
-Come on.

613
00:57:32,086 --> 00:57:34,365
Are the cauldrons boiling?

614
00:57:35,046 --> 00:57:36,765
Have the meals been prepared?

615
00:57:40,366 --> 00:57:44,285
The Sultan of eleven months
has arrived, how can we sleep?

616
00:57:47,366 --> 00:57:51,365
Don't sleep lazily, get up and do good deeds.

617
00:57:54,246 --> 00:57:58,765
Cerkutay will wake you up, don't worry.

618
00:58:07,366 --> 00:58:09,805
Peace be upon you. No. Sit. Sit.

619
00:58:09,806 --> 00:58:11,245
Peace be upon you too, my Bey.

620
00:58:11,555 --> 00:58:14,725
-Peace be upon you.
-Peace be upon you too.

621
00:58:23,646 --> 00:58:29,405
We have gone through many storms and troubles.

622
00:58:30,566 --> 00:58:33,285
But thankfully.

623
00:58:33,566 --> 00:58:36,445
...Allah always provided for us.

624
00:58:37,486 --> 00:58:40,565
Today we are in this table

625
00:58:40,686 --> 00:58:44,925
...this is only Allah's gift.

626
00:58:45,126 --> 00:58:50,285
-Thank Allah.
-Thank Allah.

627
00:58:51,726 --> 00:58:53,285
Now..

628
00:58:53,726 --> 00:58:57,645
Fasting doesn't mean only hunger.

629
00:58:58,846 --> 00:59:01,485
It mean sympathizing with the hungry.

630
00:59:02,766 --> 00:59:05,005
It means fighting against your self.

631
00:59:05,686 --> 00:59:08,805
And it means patience.

632
00:59:14,566 --> 00:59:16,125
Bala.

633
00:59:16,606 --> 00:59:21,085
Without you, this house was like an orphan.

634
00:59:21,966 --> 00:59:26,005
Thankfully, my Allah spared your life for us.

635
00:59:26,246 --> 00:59:29,285
-You're here now.
-Thanks to Allah.

636
00:59:32,366 --> 00:59:35,525
Well... May the sahur be fruitful.

637
00:59:36,286 --> 00:59:38,565
In the name of Allah, the merciful, 
the compassionate.

638
00:59:39,886 --> 00:59:41,885
Enjoy your meals.

639
00:59:42,806 --> 00:59:44,765
In the name of Allah, the merciful, 
the compassionate.

640
00:59:45,366 --> 00:59:46,925
Here, my girl.

641
00:59:47,206 --> 00:59:49,325
-Here, brother.
-Thank you, brother.

642
00:59:49,446 --> 00:59:51,645
In the name of Allah, the merciful, 
the compassionate.

643
00:59:51,806 --> 00:59:54,365
-Here, sister.
-Thanks, brother.

644
00:59:54,486 --> 00:59:56,405
Thank you.

645
00:59:56,806 --> 01:00:01,085
Thanks to Allah Who provides us with Ramadan.

646
01:00:01,966 --> 01:00:04,125
-Thanks to Allah.
-Thanks to Allah.

647
01:00:05,846 --> 01:00:07,325
Thanks to Allah.

648
01:00:07,726 --> 01:00:09,805
-Bala Hatun.
-Yes, girl?

649
01:00:09,926 --> 01:00:12,205
There in the dungeon...

650
01:00:13,006 --> 01:00:15,205
Did that woman do anything to you?

651
01:00:16,046 --> 01:00:18,605
-Were you scared?
-No, girl.

652
01:00:19,646 --> 01:00:23,045
I knew I wouldn't stay in that dark dungeon.

653
01:00:24,446 --> 01:00:28,125
I have a husband who would never leave me there.

654
01:00:28,286 --> 01:00:32,285
That's right. I never would.
-Also, I have a family.

655
01:00:34,406 --> 01:00:38,845
Yes. Yet that woman must
be punished for what she did.

656
01:00:39,846 --> 01:00:42,245
We will never forget that.

657
01:00:43,166 --> 01:00:44,685
She will be.

658
01:00:49,406 --> 01:00:53,125
Holofira, you needn't
have interrupted your sleep.

659
01:00:53,446 --> 01:00:56,525
I didn't want to leave you
alone during your first sahur.

660
01:00:56,846 --> 01:01:00,365
Besides, I want to fast too.

661
01:01:00,406 --> 01:01:01,485
No.

662
01:01:01,646 --> 01:01:04,885
Holofira, you can fast if you want.

663
01:01:05,006 --> 01:01:08,885
She can't. You are pregnant, my dear.

664
01:01:08,966 --> 01:01:11,445
Next time, God willing.

665
01:01:11,606 --> 01:01:15,365
Oh, I almost forgot that.
My mother is right. You can't.

666
01:01:17,606 --> 01:01:18,925
You forgot?

667
01:01:28,366 --> 01:01:29,725
No, Holofira.

668
01:01:29,886 --> 01:01:33,205
You mentioned fasting all of a sudden.

669
01:01:33,366 --> 01:01:36,525
So I got surprised. That's why I said so.

670
01:01:36,766 --> 01:01:38,765
You should eat, my wife.

671
01:01:39,006 --> 01:01:42,845
You should eat in the morning,
in the evening and even at noon.

672
01:01:43,006 --> 01:01:46,445
You have a good appetite these
days. You should eat all the time.

673
01:01:49,926 --> 01:01:52,085
-Brother.
-Brother.

674
01:01:53,526 --> 01:01:57,925
-Are you watching what I eat now, Orhan? -Oh no.

675
01:01:58,246 --> 01:01:59,965
-Brother.
-Sister.

676
01:02:00,086 --> 01:02:03,365
Just eat. It gets worse as you keep talking.

677
01:02:09,526 --> 01:02:13,205
Sister Meryem, pour water
in this for my brother to drink.

678
01:02:13,566 --> 01:02:17,565
Obviously, what he eats today
will burn his stomach tomorrow.

679
01:02:17,606 --> 01:02:19,845
-Alaaddin.
-It will.

680
01:02:20,006 --> 01:02:21,085
Here, brother.

681
01:02:29,486 --> 01:02:31,925
Praise be, Praise be.

682
01:02:32,446 --> 01:02:36,365
Thanks to Allah, we have peace again.

683
01:02:37,246 --> 01:02:42,165
Years ago, a fire broke out in our family.

684
01:02:43,286 --> 01:02:47,245
The ashes of that fire have
turned into a garden of roses now.

685
01:02:47,646 --> 01:02:49,045
Right, Bala?

686
01:02:53,606 --> 01:02:56,525
We have something to tell you.

687
01:02:56,966 --> 01:03:00,045
It's hard to say it.

688
01:03:00,526 --> 01:03:03,405
But it is true.

689
01:03:04,286 --> 01:03:06,845
Your sister Halime...

690
01:03:09,526 --> 01:03:11,525
Halime is alive.

691
01:03:15,246 --> 01:03:18,645
What?

692
01:03:19,246 --> 01:03:20,805
She's alive.

693
01:03:28,286 --> 01:03:29,765
How?

694
01:03:46,726 --> 01:03:48,805
Come, Ayaz Bey.

695
01:03:49,726 --> 01:03:51,325
Tell me.

696
01:03:52,246 --> 01:03:54,645
Did Osman Bey invite you?

697
01:03:56,006 --> 01:03:57,845
Yes, Commander Ulugan.

698
01:03:58,446 --> 01:04:01,805
But I will stand with you.

699
01:04:02,246 --> 01:04:06,205
I'm pledging loyalty to you
and Ilbay Bey from Kayi blood.

700
01:04:06,526 --> 01:04:08,565
You chose the right way, Ayaz Bey.

701
01:04:08,766 --> 01:04:11,725
Your loyalty will definitely be rewarded.

702
01:04:17,486 --> 01:04:20,165
Whoever doesn't get under my wings...

703
01:04:20,686 --> 01:04:23,725
...will burn to ashes with my wrath.

704
01:04:29,886 --> 01:04:33,645
But you will have a long life, Ayaz.

705
01:04:35,086 --> 01:04:36,725
Now tell me.

706
01:04:37,366 --> 01:04:40,245
Where did Osman want to meet you?

707
01:04:40,486 --> 01:04:42,045
In Serinsu.

708
01:04:42,166 --> 01:04:44,405
All the Beys are going to gather there.

709
01:04:44,406 --> 01:04:46,405
Osman will be there too.

710
01:04:49,286 --> 01:04:52,685
You're doing bigger things than yourself, Ayaz.

711
01:04:53,446 --> 01:04:54,605
Now go.

712
01:04:55,046 --> 01:05:00,005
Go where Osman wants to meet
as if nothing had happened here.

713
01:05:04,646 --> 01:05:06,565
When I arrive in there,

714
01:05:07,246 --> 01:05:08,965
..be careful.

715
01:05:09,206 --> 01:05:10,645
Find a cover.

716
01:05:10,806 --> 01:05:13,205
Protect yourself. Don't be killed.

717
01:05:14,926 --> 01:05:19,245
In that council, Osman's head will be cut off.

718
01:05:20,846 --> 01:05:25,205
You shouldn't kill the
other Turkmen Beys either.

719
01:05:25,446 --> 01:05:26,925
Don't be worrying.

720
01:05:27,246 --> 01:05:29,245
We need them alive.

721
01:05:30,206 --> 01:05:32,845
Your reward won't be only the gold.

722
01:05:33,166 --> 01:05:35,205
When you do what we say.

723
01:05:35,886 --> 01:05:38,765
...the castle of Mekece
will be under your command.

724
01:05:38,766 --> 01:05:42,165
-You won't live in a tent anymore.
-Thank you.

725
01:05:42,526 --> 01:05:46,405
Don't worry. Osman will notice nothing.

726
01:05:47,126 --> 01:05:49,085
Now excuse me.

727
01:05:51,526 --> 01:05:53,845
You may leave, Ayaz Bey.

728
01:06:04,966 --> 01:06:10,045
The easiest thing in these
lands are buying men, Ilbay.

729
01:06:10,326 --> 01:06:14,445
Akca's dog will bring death for Osman.

730
01:06:32,726 --> 01:06:34,725
The demon called Sofia...

731
01:06:35,006 --> 01:06:39,725
...has kept our sister away
from us for all those years, huh?

732
01:06:47,566 --> 01:06:50,885
That snake is holding our sister, huh?

733
01:06:54,166 --> 01:06:56,765
Who knows what she did to her for years?

734
01:06:58,366 --> 01:07:00,645
Did she turn her against us?

735
01:07:03,526 --> 01:07:05,274
Doesn't she remember us?

736
01:07:05,286 --> 01:07:07,045
We don't know, my dear.

737
01:07:08,046 --> 01:07:11,485
That snake break our peace and order.

738
01:07:12,286 --> 01:07:15,205
She threw us into the darkness of longing.

739
01:07:17,966 --> 01:07:20,005
Sofia is the key of the secret.

740
01:07:21,326 --> 01:07:22,925
We have to catch her.

741
01:07:23,006 --> 01:07:27,205
Yes, but Sofia knows we'll come for her.

742
01:07:27,326 --> 01:07:30,085
She's going to take measures. It won't be easy.

743
01:07:30,286 --> 01:07:34,765
Even if she goes into a rat
hole, we will find her, mother.

744
01:07:35,446 --> 01:07:40,845
We'll make her suffer much more
than she made us and you suffer.

745
01:07:42,286 --> 01:07:44,485
Speaking of Sofia...

746
01:07:47,766 --> 01:07:50,365
Meryem found this near the cabin.

747
01:07:51,286 --> 01:07:54,205
The sign doesn't look familiar.

748
01:07:54,646 --> 01:07:57,045
It's not from these lands, obviously.

749
01:08:13,766 --> 01:08:16,205
This belongs to Sofia. I saw it in the dungeon.

750
01:08:20,526 --> 01:08:23,165
What is it. Alaaddin?
-I checked, but...

751
01:08:23,246 --> 01:08:25,125
It look complicated, my Bey.

752
01:08:25,606 --> 01:08:27,725
But I will figure out.

753
01:08:30,286 --> 01:08:32,165
Can I have a look?

754
01:08:39,645 --> 01:08:42,285
This is Healer Martin's mark.

755
01:08:42,526 --> 01:08:46,205
He used to visit the temples
and take care of the sick children.

756
01:08:46,685 --> 01:08:48,645
Do you know where he is?

757
01:08:49,126 --> 01:08:50,604
I do.

758
01:08:51,765 --> 01:08:55,765
Maybe, this is the key
that will lead us to Sofia.

759
01:08:56,446 --> 01:09:00,604
Bala, Alaaddin. Visit that healer.

760
01:09:01,926 --> 01:09:05,444
Don't worry. Halime will join our table one day.

761
01:09:05,566 --> 01:09:08,885
We'll take back Halime and our tribe.

762
01:09:29,046 --> 01:09:33,285
I'm taking medicine. Why
do I still have this headache?

763
01:09:42,606 --> 01:09:45,165
Today, you're going to die.

764
01:09:45,486 --> 01:09:47,085
My Halime, is that you?

765
01:09:48,326 --> 01:09:49,604
Mother.

766
01:09:51,966 --> 01:09:53,245
Mother.

767
01:09:54,166 --> 01:09:56,325
Everything was almost over today.

768
01:09:58,726 --> 01:10:00,965
But I can't.

769
01:10:03,686 --> 01:10:09,605
Like the sword was going to
stick into me instead of Bala.

770
01:10:13,006 --> 01:10:15,845
I don't want, but...

771
01:10:17,246 --> 01:10:18,845
...I can't help it.

772
01:10:21,046 --> 01:10:23,885
I feel like I'm betraying my aunt.

773
01:10:29,806 --> 01:10:32,965
If you hurt my Halime

774
01:10:36,326 --> 01:10:38,085
My God.

775
01:10:39,886 --> 01:10:42,365
When will this suffering end?

776
01:10:54,806 --> 01:10:57,165
I don't know..

777
01:10:58,286 --> 01:11:00,525
...whether you are good or bad for me.

778
01:11:04,166 --> 01:11:06,285
I should visit Healer Martin.

779
01:11:10,406 --> 01:11:11,605
Meryem.

780
01:11:11,846 --> 01:11:14,485
You didn't eat anything.
You can't fast like this.

781
01:11:14,526 --> 01:11:16,325
-Eat some...
-Bala Hatun!

782
01:11:21,526 --> 01:11:24,285
My dear, are you alright?

783
01:11:26,006 --> 01:11:27,725
Let me see you.

784
01:11:28,246 --> 01:11:30,285
Why are you crying?

785
01:11:31,246 --> 01:11:33,045
I am...

786
01:11:34,526 --> 01:11:37,685
When I saw you with the milk

787
01:11:38,406 --> 01:11:40,445
..I remembered my mother.

788
01:11:41,446 --> 01:11:43,645
I miss my mother a lot, Bala Hatun.

789
01:11:45,046 --> 01:11:47,965
My longing never ends.

790
01:11:49,886 --> 01:11:52,485
Oh my wounded bird.

791
01:11:59,806 --> 01:12:02,365
Is Allah punishing me?

792
01:12:03,326 --> 01:12:06,485
Is that why He left me alone?

793
01:12:10,326 --> 01:12:15,165
-I don't have either a mother or a father!
-Not at all.

794
01:12:15,486 --> 01:12:17,445
Don't say such things, my girl.

795
01:12:17,926 --> 01:12:22,525
Look. Our Prophet (PBUH)...

796
01:12:23,206 --> 01:12:28,005
....who Allah most cares for was an orphan.

797
01:12:29,446 --> 01:12:32,285
Allah tests His servants who He cares for.

798
01:12:32,726 --> 01:12:35,565
You aren't alone, anyway. I told you many times.

799
01:12:35,846 --> 01:12:37,845
You are our girl.

800
01:12:38,246 --> 01:12:42,805
I don't have two but three daughters now.

801
01:12:46,606 --> 01:12:47,885
Three?

802
01:12:48,206 --> 01:12:50,405
I mean Halime.

803
01:12:53,486 --> 01:12:57,325
Come on, drink milk.
Azan (caller for prayer) will be recited shortly.

804
01:12:57,325 --> 01:12:58,995
Don't stay hungry.

805
01:13:22,966 --> 01:13:24,845
Osman..

806
01:13:25,526 --> 01:13:27,685
...is smarter than I thought.

807
01:13:27,806 --> 01:13:32,085
Despite all his wounds and weakness,

808
01:13:32,446 --> 01:13:34,325
...his mind never leaves him.

809
01:13:34,686 --> 01:13:39,165
We thought he would save
his alps and Beys in captivity.

810
01:13:39,526 --> 01:13:42,845
But he's gaining power from beyond the borders.

811
01:13:43,006 --> 01:13:44,645
If he were smart, Ulugan,

812
01:13:44,806 --> 01:13:49,115
...he wouldn't rely on those rebels
who care about only gold and money.

813
01:13:49,115 --> 01:13:52,125
He's smart but desperate.

814
01:13:52,846 --> 01:13:59,205
And it's his despair that will
cut off his head here today.

815
01:14:00,126 --> 01:14:03,075
Tell nokers (Mongolian soldiers)
to take positions, Altuga.

816
01:14:03,086 --> 01:14:04,765
As you order, Ulugan.

817
01:14:05,326 --> 01:14:06,965
Come on.

818
01:14:16,486 --> 01:14:18,405
-Son.
My Bey.

819
01:14:18,606 --> 01:14:21,245
Why have you got a sullen face?

820
01:14:22,526 --> 01:14:26,285
Ayaz Bey is alright. But
the other rebellious beys...

821
01:14:27,006 --> 01:14:29,445
I don't know if we should trust them.

822
01:14:30,606 --> 01:14:35,805
It seems you still have my words in your heart.

823
01:14:35,926 --> 01:14:40,485
Well... A Bey should act
with suspicion all the time.

824
01:14:41,326 --> 01:14:46,965
From now on, what we
expect from others isn't trust.

825
01:14:47,486 --> 01:14:51,285
We just expect them to take the right side.

826
01:14:52,206 --> 01:14:55,045
Okay, my Bey.

827
01:15:01,606 --> 01:15:04,965
God is my witness that this is the best quality.

828
01:15:20,846 --> 01:15:23,525
Healer must be around here.

829
01:15:23,966 --> 01:15:27,125
You said it was long before.
You're sure, aren't you?

830
01:15:27,366 --> 01:15:30,285
I'm sure, mother. We're almost there.

831
01:15:30,366 --> 01:15:32,485
Let's pass through this street.

832
01:16:09,086 --> 01:16:13,165
I don't feel well, healer Martin.

833
01:16:16,846 --> 01:16:18,645
I see dreams.

834
01:16:19,726 --> 01:16:22,125
I see dreams even without sleeping.

835
01:16:23,086 --> 01:16:24,845
I don't know...

836
01:16:26,246 --> 01:16:29,405
...whether my visions are my memories...

837
01:16:30,046 --> 01:16:32,965
...or just dreams.

838
01:16:34,046 --> 01:16:36,365
Everything is so confusing.

839
01:16:37,566 --> 01:16:40,205
I listen to someone else's life.

840
01:16:41,486 --> 01:16:45,885
But that person is me in my dreams.

841
01:16:47,926 --> 01:16:50,565
I'm from Byzantine.

842
01:16:51,406 --> 01:16:53,325
I'm a Christian.

843
01:16:53,926 --> 01:16:56,085
But what I see...

844
01:17:00,486 --> 01:17:03,725
Are you taking medicine regularly, Poena?

845
01:17:06,686 --> 01:17:08,685
What is it in this bottle?

846
01:17:09,406 --> 01:17:13,325
When I drink this, none of these happens.

847
01:17:15,046 --> 01:17:16,925
What are you making this of?

848
01:17:19,606 --> 01:17:23,685
I don't understand whether this
medicine is good or bad for me.

849
01:17:25,446 --> 01:17:28,365
Why am I seeing these when I don't take it?

850
01:17:29,366 --> 01:17:31,005
Please tell me.

851
01:17:31,566 --> 01:17:33,165
Why?

852
01:17:38,686 --> 01:17:42,485
This street. I'm sure. One of the shops here.

853
01:17:56,806 --> 01:17:58,485
This is it.

854
01:18:11,446 --> 01:18:14,965
-The same mark.
-Come on then.

855
01:18:20,286 --> 01:18:22,125
In this...

856
01:18:25,566 --> 01:18:27,485
Anyone here?

857
01:18:33,566 --> 01:18:36,885
Bala... Bala..

858
01:19:03,046 --> 01:19:04,725
What do you want?

859
01:19:06,006 --> 01:19:08,485
May Jesus Christ bless you, healer Martin.

860
01:19:08,686 --> 01:19:10,725
We have questions for you.

861
01:19:15,286 --> 01:19:18,285
This bottle was taken from you, right?

862
01:19:33,206 --> 01:19:36,125
You are true Turkmen warriors...

863
01:19:36,486 --> 01:19:43,045
...who are unique and have
solid natures like mountain ranges.

864
01:19:43,846 --> 01:19:45,285
Welcome.

865
01:19:45,566 --> 01:19:48,765
-Thank you, Osman Bey.
-Thank you, but...

866
01:19:49,526 --> 01:19:54,525
We asked Boran Bey but he
said he was just a messenger.

867
01:19:55,206 --> 01:19:58,765
Tell me, Osman Bey. Why did you call us?

868
01:19:59,806 --> 01:20:06,365
Mongolians who cause troubles in the frontiers
and attempt to harm our lives and lands...

869
01:20:06,926 --> 01:20:09,805
...should leave these lands in no time.

870
01:20:10,206 --> 01:20:14,805
I'm here to say that you and I should
follow the same path for this cause.

871
01:20:15,046 --> 01:20:19,045
You're telling us to stand behind
you with all our forces, huh?

872
01:20:19,446 --> 01:20:21,725
No, no.

873
01:20:22,686 --> 01:20:26,205
I'm not telling you to stand
behind me or obey me.

874
01:20:30,366 --> 01:20:34,125
I'm saying we should walk
shoulder-to-shoulder all together.

875
01:20:34,766 --> 01:20:39,245
I'm saying we should clear
these dark clouds all together.

876
01:20:42,886 --> 01:20:46,445
Mongolians are cause troubles
only for the states, Osman Bey.

877
01:20:46,646 --> 01:20:50,085
We just loot here and there.

878
01:20:50,326 --> 01:20:52,645
Mongolians can't find us.

879
01:20:52,926 --> 01:20:55,405
Karesi, Candar, Germiya

880
01:20:55,966 --> 01:20:57,765
...and Kayi.

881
01:20:58,606 --> 01:21:03,645
Mongolians attack the states first, of course.

882
01:21:05,006 --> 01:21:07,005
But remember this.

883
01:21:07,526 --> 01:21:09,885
All those Beys pledged loyalty.

884
01:21:10,766 --> 01:21:12,525
You know me well.

885
01:21:12,846 --> 01:21:15,005
I don't pledge loyalty to anyone.

886
01:21:16,326 --> 01:21:20,125
I would sacrifice my head and life...

887
01:21:20,846 --> 01:21:22,845
...but never kneel.

888
01:21:24,846 --> 01:21:25,885
Now...

889
01:21:27,566 --> 01:21:29,525
...this land's last castle is mine.

890
01:21:41,406 --> 01:21:43,165
The last banner is my banner.

891
01:21:44,566 --> 01:21:46,245
If we fall..

892
01:21:48,446 --> 01:21:52,805
...then the Mongols will march on Turkmens.

893
01:21:56,486 --> 01:21:59,725
When they can't see a state they can take over..

894
01:22:01,366 --> 01:22:03,165
...they will attack you.

895
01:22:03,846 --> 01:22:05,805
Keep talking, Osman

896
01:22:06,366 --> 01:22:08,725
Waste your last breath on this struggle.

897
01:22:08,766 --> 01:22:13,365
Altuga, remember. Beys won't get hurt.

898
01:22:19,726 --> 01:22:22,125
As I said, the bottle is mine.

899
01:22:23,966 --> 01:22:26,245
But I didn't make the medicine inside.

900
01:22:28,406 --> 01:22:32,045
Why would someone put medicine in your bottle?

901
01:22:32,046 --> 01:22:35,405
-Ask where you found it.
-Don't lie.

902
01:22:38,166 --> 01:22:41,685
Princess Sofia. She is our friend.

903
01:22:42,126 --> 01:22:44,565
She said that only you can know this.

904
01:22:58,406 --> 01:23:00,405
I think you have another guest.

905
01:23:39,686 --> 01:23:43,045
The rats have become a real
trouble for me. They are everywhere.

906
01:23:43,326 --> 01:23:44,965
Even the poison didn't help.

907
01:23:48,526 --> 01:23:51,525
Snake poison would surely work.

908
01:23:52,406 --> 01:23:53,925
Keep that in mind.

909
01:24:03,886 --> 01:24:08,365
Since you don't know anything, we
shouldn't keep you busy, healer Martin.

910
01:24:12,526 --> 01:24:13,765
May it be easy.

911
01:24:32,806 --> 01:24:37,645
I promise you loot, gold, and abundance.

912
01:24:38,526 --> 01:24:43,925
My path, for the name of Allah and the
glory of the Turks, is the path of shahada.

913
01:24:45,206 --> 01:24:48,685
Don't forget, this is such a path that...

914
01:24:49,326 --> 01:24:53,925
...it is the freedom cause of those who could
not be captured beyond the iron mountains.

915
01:24:53,926 --> 01:24:57,125
What you say is true Osman
Bey. If not now, then tomorrow.

916
01:24:57,126 --> 01:25:00,645
The Mongols will certainly attack us as well.
-Good.

917
01:25:00,886 --> 01:25:04,645
You said good, but we even came here secretly.

918
01:25:05,206 --> 01:25:09,245
How will we pass our Alps at
the Mongol-controlled border?

919
01:25:09,406 --> 01:25:12,885
Every difficulty has an ease.

920
01:25:18,526 --> 01:25:20,005
Just tell me you accept it.

921
01:25:20,646 --> 01:25:22,165
After you accept it..

922
01:25:22,926 --> 01:25:25,725
...there is a way to get your Alps...

923
01:25:27,446 --> 01:25:29,005
...across our border.

924
01:25:29,606 --> 01:25:31,645
First, your dog will die

925
01:25:32,686 --> 01:25:34,565
Then it's your turn Osman.

926
01:25:39,726 --> 01:25:41,965
My Shahzade!

927
01:25:41,966 --> 01:25:44,645
-Orhan!
-Alps, ambush!

928
01:25:47,366 --> 01:25:49,125
My Bey!

929
01:25:51,366 --> 01:25:53,445
Cerkutay!

930
01:25:58,486 --> 01:26:00,765
Alps!

931
01:26:02,126 --> 01:26:03,165
Alps!

932
01:26:17,686 --> 01:26:19,045
Come on

933
01:26:29,326 --> 01:26:32,365
Nokers! Let's go to the field! We will fight!

934
01:26:32,366 --> 01:26:35,925
They've hidden countless Alps in the
forest, Ulugan. There are many of them.

935
01:26:35,926 --> 01:26:39,405
I won't leave here until I tear
Osman into a thousand pieces.

936
01:26:44,606 --> 01:26:48,925
Osman and his Shahzade are
dead, Ulugan. I don't want to die here.

937
01:26:48,926 --> 01:26:52,005
-You decide what's going to happen next.
-We are retreating.

938
01:26:57,446 --> 01:27:00,925
Alps! Follow them! Go!

939
01:27:19,086 --> 01:27:21,405
When he heard Sofia's name, he was shocked.

940
01:27:22,086 --> 01:27:24,045
He will definitely make a move.

941
01:27:26,566 --> 01:27:27,645
We will wait.

942
01:27:29,326 --> 01:27:30,405
Holofira.

943
01:27:30,806 --> 01:27:32,765
My daughter.
where is your bottle?

944
01:27:32,766 --> 01:27:36,405
We are fasting, but why aren't you
eating or drinking? Drink some water.

945
01:27:36,446 --> 01:27:38,085
You are pregnant.

946
01:27:38,766 --> 01:27:42,765
I am alright mother, don't worry.
I will drink when I return to the tent.

947
01:27:50,726 --> 01:27:51,805
Someone got out.

948
01:27:54,926 --> 01:27:56,645
So, this is the rat, huh?

949
01:27:59,726 --> 01:28:02,205
We need to find out who they are.

950
01:28:06,446 --> 01:28:09,285
Martin is also going out, mother.
-Alaeddin.

951
01:28:10,126 --> 01:28:13,805
My son, follow that rat. Let's see who it is.

952
01:28:13,806 --> 01:28:17,525
Holofira, Gonca. We will follow Martin.

953
01:28:17,566 --> 01:28:20,725
-Alright mother.
-Yes mother. -Go.

954
01:28:40,846 --> 01:28:43,365
Give this to Master Sofia immediately.

955
01:29:05,886 --> 01:29:08,605
Let's follow the soldier. Let's go.

956
01:29:20,326 --> 01:29:21,805
Alaeddin Bey.

957
01:29:24,046 --> 01:29:25,965
Damn it, she noticed me!

958
01:29:26,246 --> 01:29:27,805
Move!

959
01:29:29,886 --> 01:29:30,925
Move!

960
01:29:36,926 --> 01:29:41,485
Stop! Stop! Move! -What is happening?

961
01:29:50,806 --> 01:29:51,845
Move!

962
01:29:52,846 --> 01:29:55,725
Move! Move!

963
01:29:57,646 --> 01:29:58,685
Move!

964
01:30:19,046 --> 01:30:20,525
Don't run away! Move!

965
01:30:21,566 --> 01:30:22,925
Move!

966
01:30:22,926 --> 01:30:25,285
Move, you man! Move aside!

967
01:30:29,766 --> 01:30:30,925
Where did you go?

968
01:30:31,966 --> 01:30:35,405
Even if you're hiding under
the ground, I will find you.

969
01:30:49,766 --> 01:30:55,485
You escaped now, but you will certainly
fall into my hands, rat. Certainly.

970
01:31:00,686 --> 01:31:04,605
Is everyone alright?
-Thanks to Allah, everyone is alright, my Bey.

971
01:31:06,566 --> 01:31:14,325
All the hatred that has attacked our state and
nation is not enough to scare or control us.

972
01:31:15,886 --> 01:31:20,605
It's not enough to weaken our
determination or chain our necks.

973
01:31:21,566 --> 01:31:25,445
We will teach them this in the harshest way.

974
01:31:25,846 --> 01:31:27,805
What is this situation Osman Bey?

975
01:31:28,566 --> 01:31:31,181
Did you bring us to the
place where the Mongols

976
01:31:31,193 --> 01:31:33,765
set up an ambush saying
we would meet secretly?

977
01:31:33,926 --> 01:31:35,365
What are these armors?

978
01:31:35,406 --> 01:31:39,023
If you knew there would be an
ambush why didn't you tell us?

979
01:31:39,035 --> 01:31:40,245
Don't worry.

980
01:31:41,606 --> 01:31:43,885
The Mongols do not want anything you.

981
01:31:45,406 --> 01:31:47,125
They have a problem with us.

982
01:31:48,406 --> 01:31:49,965
You asked..

983
01:31:50,806 --> 01:31:55,205
...how you would pass the Mongol route.

984
01:31:57,286 --> 01:32:04,125
This ambush is the key to all your
strength, power, and entry into our borders.

985
01:32:10,486 --> 01:32:17,245
We weren't under your command, but our respect 
for you is eternal in both worlds, Osman Bey.

986
01:32:17,446 --> 01:32:20,405
Surely, we are with you on this path. Order us.

987
01:32:20,406 --> 01:32:22,805
Thank you Ayaz Bey. Thank you.

988
01:32:24,006 --> 01:32:25,045
Now...

989
01:32:25,926 --> 01:32:27,445
...you will go to Ulugan..

990
01:32:28,126 --> 01:32:31,885
...and reveal the location where
we will meet the Turkmen Beys.

991
01:32:33,406 --> 01:32:34,605
But this..

992
01:32:36,166 --> 01:32:41,725
-What is your intention, my Bey?
-My intention is for you to gain Ulugan's trust.

993
01:32:43,206 --> 01:32:47,605
Once he sees you have sold us
out, he will want to take you to his side.

994
01:32:49,646 --> 01:32:52,485
We will learn when and
where the nokers he called...

995
01:32:52,806 --> 01:32:58,885
...from far away will enter the Kayi borders.

996
01:32:59,966 --> 01:33:06,565
You and the Turkmen Beys will enter
our lands under the guise of nokers.

997
01:33:07,086 --> 01:33:09,925
As Ulugan's army breaks apart..

998
01:33:10,846 --> 01:33:13,285
...our strength will grow

999
01:33:14,526 --> 01:33:16,045
Do your best...

1000
01:33:17,566 --> 01:33:19,005
And convince Ulugan.

1001
01:33:20,246 --> 01:33:24,045
In Serinsu, you and the Turkmen Beys.

1002
01:33:25,126 --> 01:33:27,005
You won't get hurt.

1003
01:33:28,846 --> 01:33:31,365
Ulugan's target will only be us.

1004
01:33:33,806 --> 01:33:37,205
We, with this plan...

1005
01:33:38,206 --> 01:33:40,085
...secured your safety.

1006
01:33:44,326 --> 01:33:45,445
Ayaz Bey.

1007
01:33:47,126 --> 01:33:48,245
Thank you.

1008
01:33:48,606 --> 01:33:51,045
You have also become the leader of this duty.

1009
01:33:51,046 --> 01:33:52,525
Not about me, Osman Bey.

1010
01:33:52,526 --> 01:33:56,045
This foresight is yours. I
only did what you told me.

1011
01:34:00,286 --> 01:34:01,925
Now tell me Beys.

1012
01:34:03,366 --> 01:34:06,765
In this important battle,
are you with the Turks?

1013
01:34:06,766 --> 01:34:12,125
Your sagacity won't only bring down the Mongols,
it will bring the whole world to its knees.

1014
01:34:12,126 --> 01:34:15,525
I am with you with all my strength
along with my Alps, my Bey.

1015
01:34:16,886 --> 01:34:19,885
Thank you. Thank you.

1016
01:34:22,286 --> 01:34:23,685
Ayaz Bey...

1017
01:34:24,926 --> 01:34:26,645
Now you will go to Ulugan.

1018
01:34:27,286 --> 01:34:28,605
You will learn...

1019
01:34:29,406 --> 01:34:33,405
...where and how his nokers
will pass through the borders.

1020
01:34:33,406 --> 01:34:37,165
If he asks about Orhan and me...

1021
01:34:39,006 --> 01:34:42,205
...say that we are severely wounded.
-As you order, my Bey.

1022
01:35:03,606 --> 01:35:08,285
Holofira, stay behind us. We
will first make that soldier speak.

1023
01:35:15,926 --> 01:35:19,485
Come on!

1024
01:35:28,526 --> 01:35:29,565
Dastard dog!

1025
01:35:31,286 --> 01:35:34,605
Where is the note? You will give that to us!

1026
01:35:36,366 --> 01:35:38,525
-Never!
-Speak!

1027
01:35:38,566 --> 01:35:40,205
You were going to Sofia, right?

1028
01:35:40,206 --> 01:35:42,645
You will tell us everything you know!
-Never!

1029
01:35:49,486 --> 01:35:51,045
Where is the note?

1030
01:35:58,126 --> 01:35:59,285
Holofira, read this.

1031
01:36:05,206 --> 01:36:08,405
Come to the usual place
tomorrow, it's important, it says.

1032
01:36:09,006 --> 01:36:12,005
We can only understand
this once we get there, mother.

1033
01:36:12,046 --> 01:36:15,405
But first, we need to get this to Sofia.

1034
01:36:16,926 --> 01:36:20,525
Let's dress one of the
Alps in this dog's clothes.

1035
01:36:20,686 --> 01:36:22,965
We will go after Martin tomorrow.

1036
01:36:23,006 --> 01:36:27,165
We will ambush Sofia there.
Come on. Come on, Alps.

1037
01:36:31,006 --> 01:36:34,325
My daughter, Halime, I will
take you back from that snake.

1038
01:36:34,726 --> 01:36:38,285
We will come together, my child.

1039
01:36:44,846 --> 01:36:48,405
-Are we sure Orhan and Osman are dead?
-I'm sure.

1040
01:36:48,766 --> 01:36:53,325
Those arrows could even
pierce a pig, Begum Hatun.

1041
01:36:54,846 --> 01:36:56,685
Finally, they will die.

1042
01:36:57,286 --> 01:36:59,165
Soon we will hear their sala, Begum.

1043
01:36:59,366 --> 01:37:01,885
I will send Bala back to where she came from.

1044
01:37:01,886 --> 01:37:08,165
Do not be sure they are dead
until you see Osman's corpse.

1045
01:37:19,366 --> 01:37:21,845
Ayaz Bey is here, Ulugan.

1046
01:37:22,686 --> 01:37:24,445
He wants to see you.

1047
01:37:25,166 --> 01:37:26,285
Let him in.

1048
01:37:37,886 --> 01:37:39,045
Ayaz Bey...

1049
01:37:40,006 --> 01:37:42,525
Are Osman and Orhan dead?

1050
01:37:46,406 --> 01:37:48,005
They are still breathing.

1051
01:37:49,926 --> 01:37:52,725
But they will breathe their
last, Commander Ulugan.

1052
01:37:52,886 --> 01:37:55,365
They cannot survive with those wounds.

1053
01:37:56,406 --> 01:37:59,005
You have done a great job, Ayaz Bey.

1054
01:37:59,846 --> 01:38:01,605
This happened thanks to you.

1055
01:38:02,606 --> 01:38:07,925
If Osman had gathered the Beys to his side,
it would have been hard to defeat him.

1056
01:38:08,966 --> 01:38:10,725
Thank you, Ilbay Bey.

1057
01:38:10,926 --> 01:38:14,365
But Alaeddin and Bala Hatun are still alive.

1058
01:38:14,646 --> 01:38:17,005
I heard you lost many nokers.

1059
01:38:17,246 --> 01:38:18,845
That dog..

1060
01:38:20,206 --> 01:38:21,365
...and that Hatun.

1061
01:38:23,486 --> 01:38:27,125
Do you think they can stand against me Ayaz?

1062
01:38:29,446 --> 01:38:31,925
My nokers have already set out.

1063
01:38:32,726 --> 01:38:34,565
They will be here soon.

1064
01:38:35,286 --> 01:38:37,605
Everyone in that family will die.

1065
01:38:38,046 --> 01:38:40,645
If you allow me, I can set out and meet them.

1066
01:38:40,646 --> 01:38:41,885
Which way will they come?

1067
01:38:42,246 --> 01:38:44,245
Do you think we do not know the way?

1068
01:38:44,486 --> 01:38:48,845
Why would you show us the way, Ayaz?
-I... -You...

1069
01:38:50,126 --> 01:38:53,725
Do as you are told, don't
interfere with anything else.

1070
01:38:54,526 --> 01:38:56,765
Now go, wait for my order.

1071
01:38:58,046 --> 01:38:59,925
As you order, Commander Ulugan.

1072
01:39:15,046 --> 01:39:17,285
What am I going to say to Osman Bey now?

1073
01:39:17,486 --> 01:39:20,245
All those Alps are going
to die because I failed.

1074
01:39:21,326 --> 01:39:24,045
Altuga... Where are my nokers?

1075
01:39:24,446 --> 01:39:28,045
They are almost at the Karacahisar
borders, Commander Ulugan.

1076
01:39:28,686 --> 01:39:30,405
What are you doing here?

1077
01:39:32,686 --> 01:39:35,165
I dropped my hat. I was taking it back.

1078
01:39:39,966 --> 01:39:44,365
Come, you dastards.

1079
01:39:52,446 --> 01:39:53,565
Thank you mother.

1080
01:39:55,606 --> 01:39:56,645
Thank you mother.

1081
01:39:57,926 --> 01:39:59,805
Hatun. -Thank you.

1082
01:40:00,886 --> 01:40:02,765
My daughter.

1083
01:40:04,726 --> 01:40:06,485
In the name of Allah, the merciful, 
the compassionate.

1084
01:40:09,926 --> 01:40:11,805
May Allah accept it. -Aameen.

1085
01:40:14,726 --> 01:40:15,765
Let's start eating.

1086
01:40:16,406 --> 01:40:18,365
In the name of Allah, the merciful, 
the compassionate.

1087
01:40:27,086 --> 01:40:28,125
My Bey...

1088
01:40:28,926 --> 01:40:31,965
We also left the Alps to watch Martin.

1089
01:40:31,966 --> 01:40:34,005
They will report everything he does.

1090
01:40:35,326 --> 01:40:37,245
What about the one hiding inside?

1091
01:40:38,326 --> 01:40:41,245
-Is there any news from that person, Alaeddin?
-No, my Bey.

1092
01:40:42,126 --> 01:40:45,165
It's like the ground split
open and swallowed them.

1093
01:40:45,446 --> 01:40:48,645
Since Martin hid that person
he must know who it is.

1094
01:40:49,286 --> 01:40:53,045
When we catch him, we will make
him talk and find out, God willing.

1095
01:40:53,926 --> 01:40:54,965
Right.

1096
01:40:55,246 --> 01:40:59,085
Tomorrow, when they meet, both
Martin and Sofia will be in our hands.

1097
01:40:59,406 --> 01:41:00,445
God willing.

1098
01:41:04,726 --> 01:41:06,325
My Halime.

1099
01:41:06,886 --> 01:41:08,605
We'll find my daughter.

1100
01:41:08,966 --> 01:41:12,485
I'll make Sofia suffer much
more than she made me suffer.

1101
01:41:12,846 --> 01:41:16,125
Don't worry. We'll do such things to her...

1102
01:41:17,326 --> 01:41:22,165
...that she can't go anywhere
before she pays for what she did.

1103
01:41:22,406 --> 01:41:26,565
I will cut off her flesh!

1104
01:41:27,326 --> 01:41:29,965
I'll make her an example for everyone!

1105
01:41:34,926 --> 01:41:37,485
By your leave, I should go.

1106
01:41:39,566 --> 01:41:41,125
I have a headache.

1107
01:41:41,406 --> 01:41:44,925
Of course, girl. You may leave.

1108
01:41:45,486 --> 01:41:48,365
Is it because it's the first day of fasting?

1109
01:41:48,646 --> 01:41:50,165
Or are you sick?

1110
01:41:51,686 --> 01:41:54,725
I feel sick, but it will be alright when I rest.

1111
01:42:15,486 --> 01:42:18,605
If they catch Martin, they will find me too.

1112
01:42:18,766 --> 01:42:23,005
If my aunt is caught, they will kill her too.

1113
01:42:24,246 --> 01:42:28,645
When Turks killed your family in front of
your eyes, you couldn't stand it, Poena.

1114
01:42:28,806 --> 01:42:31,965
You were too young and saw unreal things.

1115
01:42:32,206 --> 01:42:35,485
Sofia was worried that you'd lose your mind.

1116
01:42:36,366 --> 01:42:38,765
So I worked hard to make this medicine.

1117
01:42:40,006 --> 01:42:42,725
I couldn't find a definite cure, unfortunately.

1118
01:42:43,486 --> 01:42:46,685
If you don't take it, you will
have those dreams again.

1119
01:42:49,486 --> 01:42:50,925
Well..

1120
01:42:51,446 --> 01:42:54,405
Is it normal that I see what I hear?

1121
01:42:54,806 --> 01:42:56,965
You're affected by what you hear.

1122
01:42:57,046 --> 01:43:00,925
Those aren't your dreams.
Your mind is playing games.

1123
01:43:04,206 --> 01:43:05,525
Well..

1124
01:43:05,806 --> 01:43:07,245
What if I don't take it?

1125
01:43:07,486 --> 01:43:10,125
-What happens?
-You'll lose your mind.

1126
01:43:10,126 --> 01:43:13,125
Poena? See? It has already started.

1127
01:43:24,806 --> 01:43:27,005
Oh good-hearted Sofia.

1128
01:43:27,926 --> 01:43:30,645
Her biggest fear is you getting sick again.

1129
01:43:31,046 --> 01:43:33,525
Don't forget to take your medicine.

1130
01:43:34,286 --> 01:43:37,285
You're so precious to her. Poena.

1131
01:43:40,806 --> 01:43:43,165
My aunt is my precious too.

1132
01:43:46,566 --> 01:43:48,525
I will ruin your plans.

1133
01:43:49,566 --> 01:43:51,645
I will inform my aunt.

1134
01:43:52,126 --> 01:43:57,205
You won't be able to catch Martin or my aunt.

1135
01:43:58,526 --> 01:44:00,645
I won't let that happen.

1136
01:44:10,966 --> 01:44:13,525
Every day Osman and his family are happy,

1137
01:44:13,646 --> 01:44:16,245
...I drown in grief, Sofia

1138
01:44:19,806 --> 01:44:22,845
This is Commander Lukas' sword.

1139
01:44:24,646 --> 01:44:29,005
Like he wants me to kill Osman
and help his soul to find peace.

1140
01:44:30,926 --> 01:44:34,405
Whoever waits patiently wins, Hristo.

1141
01:44:39,126 --> 01:44:41,765
These are their last peaceful days.

1142
01:44:42,686 --> 01:44:43,885
Soon

1143
01:44:44,286 --> 01:44:47,845
...our glasses will be filled with blood.

1144
01:44:52,366 --> 01:44:55,565
Lady Sofia, he's brought important news for you.

1145
01:45:14,166 --> 01:45:16,245
You may leave.

1146
01:45:27,806 --> 01:45:29,645
Meryem.

1147
01:45:35,726 --> 01:45:37,885
Where are you going?

1148
01:45:44,086 --> 01:45:46,885
I couldn't stay in my tent.

1149
01:45:47,326 --> 01:45:50,445
I still had a headache
so I wanted to take a walk.

1150
01:45:55,646 --> 01:45:57,605
Come here.

1151
01:45:58,886 --> 01:46:00,685
You don't have a fever.

1152
01:46:01,046 --> 01:46:04,645
We can tell Alaaddin Bey to
prepare some medicine for you.

1153
01:46:05,606 --> 01:46:07,805
No, it'll be fine when I walk a little.

1154
01:46:08,086 --> 01:46:13,485
Mother, she keeps telling it will fine but
she doesn't take a good care of herself.

1155
01:46:17,126 --> 01:46:20,765
Then we will take care of her, Fatma.

1156
01:46:21,526 --> 01:46:23,965
She's a girl of this tribe now.

1157
01:46:25,286 --> 01:46:28,685
Thank you, but I'm really fine.

1158
01:46:29,046 --> 01:46:31,485
I need some fresh air.

1159
01:46:31,806 --> 01:46:34,085
Let's get fresh air together then.

1160
01:46:34,726 --> 01:46:36,885
Besides, tell me...

1161
01:46:37,126 --> 01:46:39,885
What do you want to eat in sahur?

1162
01:46:40,126 --> 01:46:43,965
It doesn't matter as long as you cook, mother.

1163
01:46:44,406 --> 01:46:46,205
My pretty daughter.

1164
01:46:50,926 --> 01:46:55,645
And you, Meryem? I can't cook as
well as your deceased grandmother, but...

1165
01:46:55,806 --> 01:46:58,405
...tell me if you crave something.

1166
01:46:58,926 --> 01:47:02,165
Thank you, Bala Hatun. I don't crave anything.

1167
01:47:04,166 --> 01:47:07,405
Well... It seems you're going to be ill.

1168
01:47:08,846 --> 01:47:12,125
Fatma, don't stay here
for long. Go to your tent.

1169
01:47:12,326 --> 01:47:15,885
Don't leave her. If she gets
worse, we'll call your brother.

1170
01:47:15,966 --> 01:47:19,845
Don't worry, mother. I will keep my eyes on her.

1171
01:47:20,966 --> 01:47:23,365
She's my sister now.

1172
01:47:28,646 --> 01:47:30,965
-Come on.
-Come on.

1173
01:47:44,286 --> 01:47:45,765
Brother.

1174
01:47:46,286 --> 01:47:50,885
You said even the sharpest
spears can't pierce it.

1175
01:47:51,406 --> 01:47:53,565
You gave us an armor.

1176
01:47:53,846 --> 01:47:57,445
And you sent my Bey and
me into the enemy's range.

1177
01:47:58,326 --> 01:48:01,285
-And, brother?
And, Alaaddin...

1178
01:48:01,846 --> 01:48:04,525
Even with the first arrow hitting my back...

1179
01:48:05,046 --> 01:48:06,525
I thought...

1180
01:48:07,046 --> 01:48:09,125
"It's over, Orhan."

1181
01:48:10,086 --> 01:48:13,685
I thought my heart was broken into two.

1182
01:48:20,526 --> 01:48:21,845
Brother.

1183
01:48:22,606 --> 01:48:24,725
In the world...
-Yes?

1184
01:48:25,406 --> 01:48:30,725
Is there an arrow which can break
this heart harder than even rock?

1185
01:48:31,886 --> 01:48:33,285
I don't know, brother.

1186
01:48:33,286 --> 01:48:35,365
Harder than even rock?
-Yes.

1187
01:48:36,286 --> 01:48:40,405
Harder than even rock,
huh? Harder than even rock!

1188
01:48:44,206 --> 01:48:46,845
Harder than even rock, huh?

1189
01:48:55,206 --> 01:48:59,885
My sons, may Allah keep
you away from grief and sorrow.

1190
01:49:01,766 --> 01:49:04,845
May the light in your eyes never die.

1191
01:49:05,206 --> 01:49:07,525
-Aameen, my Bey.
-Thank you, my Bey.

1192
01:49:07,526 --> 01:49:09,085
Aameen.

1193
01:49:12,126 --> 01:49:14,325
Do I have permission, my Bey?

1194
01:49:15,606 --> 01:49:17,725
Come in, Boran.

1195
01:49:22,126 --> 01:49:24,805
My Bey, from Ayaz Bey.

1196
01:49:39,246 --> 01:49:41,805
My Bey, what's the news?

1197
01:49:42,046 --> 01:49:43,765
Do we know anything?

1198
01:49:44,166 --> 01:49:45,765
Yes, we do.

1199
01:49:49,966 --> 01:49:51,725
Ulugan's nokers...

1200
01:49:52,806 --> 01:49:56,125
...are going to enter our lands
through Karacahisar tomorrow.

1201
01:50:03,286 --> 01:50:07,645
Tell all the Turkmen Beys
to make preparations quickly.

1202
01:50:07,926 --> 01:50:10,365
And wait for us beyond the borders.

1203
01:50:10,566 --> 01:50:14,765
We'll take action all together after sahur.

1204
01:50:15,486 --> 01:50:17,845
-As you order, my Bey.
-As you order, my Bey.

1205
01:50:18,126 --> 01:50:19,685
As you order, my Bey.

1206
01:50:28,006 --> 01:50:29,125
Osman Bey.

1207
01:50:41,606 --> 01:50:43,525
Osman Bey.

1208
01:50:44,006 --> 01:50:45,445
Welcome.

1209
01:50:45,606 --> 01:50:49,205
Did you take measures as I warned you?

1210
01:50:49,806 --> 01:50:51,405
We did, Osman Bey.

1211
01:50:51,566 --> 01:50:54,085
All our alps are hiding in the woods.

1212
01:50:54,326 --> 01:50:57,085
-Waiting for our call.
-Alright.

1213
01:50:57,726 --> 01:50:59,285
Alright.

1214
01:51:00,726 --> 01:51:06,445
Now we'll cut off the snake's head and skin it.

1215
01:51:07,606 --> 01:51:12,405
Then your alps will enter
my lands with a disguise.

1216
01:51:12,566 --> 01:51:14,325
As you order, my Bey.

1217
01:51:17,006 --> 01:51:18,805
-Boran.
-My Bey.

1218
01:51:19,686 --> 01:51:21,565
Go check it out.

1219
01:51:22,366 --> 01:51:26,885
Tell me how many and how cautious they are.

1220
01:51:27,126 --> 01:51:29,085
As you order, my Bey.

1221
01:51:41,666 --> 01:51:44,485
Near Byzantine Village

1222
01:51:48,086 --> 01:51:49,365
Mother.

1223
01:51:50,046 --> 01:51:51,685
You're fine, aren't you?

1224
01:51:52,006 --> 01:51:54,085
I'm both as happy as a lark...

1225
01:51:54,366 --> 01:51:56,845
...and as furious as a fire, Gonca.

1226
01:51:57,446 --> 01:51:59,005
For years..

1227
01:51:59,326 --> 01:52:03,085
My child was alive but I mourned for her.

1228
01:52:04,086 --> 01:52:07,525
Finding the missing is a great gift, mother.

1229
01:52:07,846 --> 01:52:12,325
For sure we'll save
our sister from those dogs.

1230
01:52:12,766 --> 01:52:14,325
We will.

1231
01:52:14,646 --> 01:52:17,445
Like the whole world got shaken...

1232
01:52:18,086 --> 01:52:20,405
...and resettled.

1233
01:52:21,486 --> 01:52:24,725
Like the wound in my heart never bled.

1234
01:52:41,766 --> 01:52:45,525
-My Bey.
-Tell me how many they are.

1235
01:52:51,446 --> 01:52:53,525
Why do you keep silent?

1236
01:52:55,246 --> 01:52:57,765
Those dogs are too many, my Bey.

1237
01:52:58,246 --> 01:53:00,045
They have a regular army.

1238
01:53:00,206 --> 01:53:02,485
Hundreds walking one after another.

1239
01:53:02,486 --> 01:53:05,405
They're going beyond mountains
and walking towards the pass.

1240
01:53:05,446 --> 01:53:07,925
They'll be here before long, my Bey.

1241
01:53:10,606 --> 01:53:13,285
Thanks to Allah, we have
a chance to swing swords.

1242
01:53:59,406 --> 01:54:02,085
Do you think we can break that army, Osman bey?

1243
01:54:02,606 --> 01:54:04,645
They are too many.

1244
01:54:07,086 --> 01:54:08,685
We will break.

1245
01:54:09,326 --> 01:54:11,765
We will burn them if we have to.

1246
01:54:12,486 --> 01:54:15,325
But we won't let them pass.

1247
01:54:18,926 --> 01:54:20,685
Tell me.

1248
01:54:22,046 --> 01:54:23,965
What do you doubt?

1249
01:54:37,246 --> 01:54:38,885
You look cheerful.

1250
01:54:38,886 --> 01:54:41,885
We're getting closer to my
sister with every step, my dear.

1251
01:54:42,006 --> 01:54:43,365
Don't worry.

1252
01:54:43,446 --> 01:54:47,605
-That day is very soon. Scholar.
-God willing. God willing.

1253
01:54:49,326 --> 01:54:52,045
I had lost my mother yesterday.

1254
01:54:53,606 --> 01:54:55,205
But today...

1255
01:54:55,846 --> 01:54:59,005
...we have a great hope right, Trickster Hatun?

1256
01:54:59,806 --> 01:55:01,245
Yes.

1257
01:55:07,926 --> 01:55:10,125
The healer is coming, mother.

1258
01:55:12,566 --> 01:55:13,805
Soon..

1259
01:55:15,126 --> 01:55:17,485
We'll be together soon, my child.

1260
01:55:19,846 --> 01:55:21,605
Let's see where he goes.

1261
01:55:22,046 --> 01:55:24,965
In the name of Allah, the merciful, 
the compassionate. Come on.

1262
01:55:34,406 --> 01:55:36,805
That is not doubt, Osman Bey. It's the truth.

1263
01:55:38,886 --> 01:55:40,325
What is this truth?

1264
01:55:41,286 --> 01:55:43,205
Tell us so we can hear it too.

1265
01:55:45,446 --> 01:55:47,805
I have no Alp who will be killed for no reason.

1266
01:55:48,766 --> 01:55:51,645
We can't fight with all these
nokers. I am not with you.

1267
01:55:57,646 --> 01:55:59,285
What are you saying, you coward?

1268
01:55:59,966 --> 01:56:03,245
Which tradition allows you to
run away from the battlefield?

1269
01:56:04,486 --> 01:56:07,205
Are you teaching us our traditions, Orhan Bey?

1270
01:56:07,646 --> 01:56:10,805
A Bey doesn't send his
Alp into a fight he can't win.

1271
01:56:11,486 --> 01:56:13,965
I will leave with my Alps as well.

1272
01:56:14,206 --> 01:56:16,405
I will rip that...
-My Shahzade.

1273
01:56:20,526 --> 01:56:24,405
Yes, a Bey doesn't send his
Alp into a fight he can't win.

1274
01:56:26,006 --> 01:56:28,725
A Bey stops the dastards from moving forward.

1275
01:56:28,886 --> 01:56:32,565
Even if he is going to die in the
end, he never lets infidels pass.

1276
01:56:32,726 --> 01:56:35,205
He does not let them trample down his honour.

1277
01:56:38,286 --> 01:56:39,965
We don't need famous Beys...

1278
01:56:41,606 --> 01:56:45,245
...we need Beys who will
follow our great cause.

1279
01:56:48,686 --> 01:56:51,725
There is no place for cowards like you...

1280
01:56:51,926 --> 01:56:53,805
..in our ranks.

1281
01:56:56,686 --> 01:56:57,885
Now get lost.

1282
01:56:59,166 --> 01:57:00,205
Get lost!

1283
01:57:06,766 --> 01:57:08,965
My Bey, allow me. I'll kill them.

1284
01:57:10,726 --> 01:57:11,845
Let them Shamil.

1285
01:57:12,766 --> 01:57:14,125
Let them

1286
01:57:21,046 --> 01:57:23,125
My Bey, the dogs are approaching.

1287
01:57:23,366 --> 01:57:26,325
The sound of their footsteps
filled the entire valley.

1288
01:57:26,766 --> 01:57:29,005
We only have a few men.

1289
01:57:29,406 --> 01:57:31,445
We are facing hundreds of nokers.

1290
01:57:34,326 --> 01:57:36,565
What are we going to do now, my Bey?

1291
01:58:04,846 --> 01:58:07,805
Come on Sofia. Come.

1292
01:58:08,126 --> 01:58:12,205
If she trusts the messenger
we sent, she will come.

1293
01:58:12,446 --> 01:58:15,685
What if she realizes we changed the messenger?

1294
01:58:32,606 --> 01:58:33,645
Tell me.

1295
01:58:33,766 --> 01:58:36,445
What is happening? Who came? What did they ask?

1296
01:58:36,606 --> 01:58:39,005
First, Poena came.

1297
01:58:39,526 --> 01:58:42,445
She asked me strange questions.
-Poena?

1298
01:58:43,286 --> 01:58:45,205
What are they talking about?

1299
01:58:48,126 --> 01:58:49,285
What did she ask?

1300
01:58:49,726 --> 01:58:51,325
She is remembering things.

1301
01:58:52,366 --> 01:58:54,525
The main issue is...

1302
01:58:55,206 --> 01:58:57,965
After she left, others came.

1303
01:58:59,086 --> 01:59:02,005
They asked about the bottles I gave you.

1304
01:59:06,606 --> 01:59:08,085
Who were they?

1305
01:59:08,886 --> 01:59:11,805
Come on! -Damn it..

1306
01:59:12,206 --> 01:59:15,525
-Sofia.
-Bala.

1307
01:59:24,126 --> 01:59:27,125
Now no one can take you from me.

1308
01:59:27,126 --> 01:59:28,765
Alps, take the healer.

1309
01:59:31,206 --> 01:59:32,565
Sofia.

1310
01:59:35,126 --> 01:59:36,325
Snake.

1311
01:59:36,606 --> 01:59:40,325
You will pay for every day
you kept my sister away from us.

1312
01:59:40,526 --> 01:59:42,485
I will kill all of you.

1313
01:59:42,646 --> 01:59:45,925
We won't kill you before you tell
us where my daughter is, Sofia.

1314
01:59:45,926 --> 01:59:48,445
But first, I will kill you.

1315
02:00:05,886 --> 02:00:08,045
It was almost over, Bala.

1316
02:00:08,126 --> 02:00:10,165
You made a big mistake by not dying.

1317
02:00:10,166 --> 02:00:13,325
You made that mistake,
Sofia. You made it by living.

1318
02:00:13,326 --> 02:00:16,925
You made it by taking my
child. I will make you regret living.

1319
02:00:48,326 --> 02:00:49,765
The game is over, Sofia.

1320
02:00:50,046 --> 02:00:51,685
Where is my daughter?

1321
02:00:51,726 --> 02:00:53,605
If you kill me..

1322
02:00:54,726 --> 02:00:58,285
...you will never learn, Bala. Come on.

1323
02:00:58,726 --> 02:00:59,765
Kill me!

1324
02:01:00,686 --> 02:01:01,725
Come on!

1325
02:01:23,326 --> 02:01:24,365
This..

1326
02:01:25,126 --> 02:01:27,485
...is the Karacahisar Castle that...

1327
02:01:28,246 --> 02:01:32,725
...Osman took with great
effort and lost with my wrath.

1328
02:01:35,326 --> 02:01:39,645
This will be the new home of my nokers, Altuga.

1329
02:01:41,046 --> 02:01:42,925
Is the castle ready? Tell me.

1330
02:01:42,966 --> 02:01:46,165
It is, Commander Ulugan. It is.

1331
02:01:46,166 --> 02:01:48,885
The food and water are all ready.

1332
02:01:49,246 --> 02:01:52,445
Our soldiers will stay here as they please.

1333
02:01:52,606 --> 02:01:56,329
From here, my army
will attack the tribe and

1334
02:01:56,341 --> 02:02:00,325
the nearby castles like
lightning with my order.

1335
02:02:01,446 --> 02:02:05,085
Once they come, I will
water these lands with blood.

1336
02:02:18,366 --> 02:02:20,685
These are Alps. What are they doing here?

1337
02:02:20,686 --> 02:02:23,805
We need to inform Ulugan. Come on!
-Come on!

1338
02:02:36,486 --> 02:02:40,325
There are Alps in the forest next
to the castle. Commander Ulugan.

1339
02:02:40,326 --> 02:02:41,144
Who are they?

1340
02:02:41,156 --> 02:02:43,645
We couldn't see their faces
from afar, Commander Ulugan.

1341
02:02:43,646 --> 02:02:46,243
Let me go and see, Ulugan.
I'll take their lives and return.

1342
02:02:46,255 --> 02:02:47,125
Stop.

1343
02:02:48,446 --> 02:02:50,085
We'll go together.

1344
02:02:52,286 --> 02:02:55,845
Let's see who these Alps
wandering in my lands are.

1345
02:02:55,846 --> 02:02:56,845
We will see.

1346
02:02:57,406 --> 02:02:58,565
To horses.

1347
02:03:33,046 --> 02:03:34,285
Osman.

1348
02:03:41,006 --> 02:03:47,005
I would never think you were dead before
I saw your and your dog's corpses but...

1349
02:03:47,726 --> 02:03:50,565
..I also didn't know you could
stand against me like that.

1350
02:03:51,566 --> 02:03:54,205
You should have been torn to pieces.

1351
02:03:54,326 --> 02:03:57,125
Your arrows can not harm us.

1352
02:03:58,046 --> 02:03:59,085
But..

1353
02:03:59,686 --> 02:04:02,485
...you will be punished by my sword of justice.

1354
02:04:03,246 --> 02:04:06,765
I... I will kill you.

1355
02:04:12,206 --> 02:04:14,285
This arrogance will kill you.

1356
02:04:15,366 --> 02:04:18,325
You are a miserable man here...

1357
02:04:18,486 --> 02:04:20,805
...but you are still being stubborn.

1358
02:04:20,806 --> 02:04:22,485
This is what our tradition is.

1359
02:04:24,286 --> 02:04:26,445
Turks never kneel before others!

1360
02:04:26,806 --> 02:04:30,005
They never receive orders from a dog.

1361
02:04:30,886 --> 02:04:34,685
And they cannot be ruled by others!
-You...

1362
02:04:36,006 --> 02:04:37,765
...will never change, Osman.

1363
02:04:39,006 --> 02:04:40,565
Even if a century passes...

1364
02:04:40,606 --> 02:04:43,605
...your arrogance and
stubbornness will remain unchanged.

1365
02:04:43,606 --> 02:04:45,165
My ancestor is Oghuz.

1366
02:04:45,806 --> 02:04:47,165
My blood is his blood.

1367
02:04:47,166 --> 02:04:50,445
My stubbornness is his stubbornness.
Let alone a hundred years...

1368
02:04:50,526 --> 02:04:52,165
...even if a thousand years pass...

1369
02:04:52,166 --> 02:04:54,005
...it will never change

1370
02:04:54,566 --> 02:04:55,765
Never!

1371
02:04:56,806 --> 02:04:58,085
But now

1372
02:04:58,526 --> 02:05:00,405
...you are facing us.

1373
02:05:02,086 --> 02:05:03,605
Now we will see you.

1374
02:05:03,886 --> 02:05:07,445
Those who hold a sword die by the sword.

1375
02:05:07,806 --> 02:05:10,725
My arrows did not kill you...

1376
02:05:13,046 --> 02:05:16,565
...but my sword will kill you now.

1377
02:05:16,646 --> 02:05:20,205
Blood! Blood!

1378
02:05:21,046 --> 02:05:22,445
We will see.

1379
02:05:35,246 --> 02:05:36,285
Meryem.

1380
02:05:37,326 --> 02:05:38,365
Are you alright?

1381
02:05:38,806 --> 02:05:39,845
I am alright.

1382
02:05:40,326 --> 02:05:41,365
I am alright.

1383
02:05:42,526 --> 02:05:44,165
You seem upset.

1384
02:05:46,206 --> 02:05:47,685
If you have a problem...

1385
02:05:48,406 --> 02:05:50,285
...tell me. I'll listen to you.

1386
02:05:57,166 --> 02:05:58,205
Walk!

1387
02:06:03,126 --> 02:06:06,645
Get up Sofia! Get up! Get up!

1388
02:06:08,966 --> 02:06:10,205
Devil!

1389
02:06:11,086 --> 02:06:12,405
It will be over today!

1390
02:06:12,886 --> 02:06:13,925
Walk!

1391
02:06:17,806 --> 02:06:19,125
Bala Hatun is coming.

1392
02:06:20,246 --> 02:06:24,725
Now no one will be able to
take you from my hands, Sofia.

1393
02:06:28,286 --> 02:06:30,405
You will tell me where my daughter is.

1394
02:06:30,486 --> 02:06:32,525
You will take me to my daughter.

1395
02:06:47,846 --> 02:06:48,885
Aunt..

1396
02:07:00,766 --> 02:07:03,725
Now no one will be able
to save you from me, Sofia.

1397
02:07:03,806 --> 02:07:06,245
You will tell me where my daughter is!

1398
02:07:12,886 --> 02:07:13,925
Never.

1399
02:07:15,806 --> 02:07:19,685
You will never learn, Bala. Never.

1400
02:07:38,726 --> 02:07:43,965
You will pay for the pain you caused
to my daughter and to my family, Sofia.

1401
02:08:10,246 --> 02:08:11,845
Are you ready Osman?

1402
02:08:12,886 --> 02:08:14,245
I am ready.

1403
02:08:17,926 --> 02:08:19,285
I am ready.

1404
02:08:19,966 --> 02:08:21,805
I always keep my promises...

1405
02:08:22,766 --> 02:08:24,765
..and take my revenge.

1406
02:08:25,046 --> 02:08:27,445
The Israfil you believe...

1407
02:08:28,166 --> 02:08:30,285
..won't blow the trumpet...

1408
02:08:31,246 --> 02:08:33,485
...but I will be your apocalypse.

1409
02:08:34,126 --> 02:08:37,725
I already killed you Osman.

1410
02:08:38,326 --> 02:08:41,245
You don't even know. Turn around.

1411
02:08:41,726 --> 02:08:43,165
And look behind you.

1412
02:08:43,166 --> 02:08:46,685
Turn around and see well how great my power is.

1413
02:08:58,726 --> 02:09:00,205
See, Osman?

1414
02:09:00,926 --> 02:09:08,005
My army which will bring the apocalypse to
your lands, your people and your race is here.

1415
02:09:09,006 --> 02:09:11,325
So, you set a trap for me, Ulugan.

1416
02:09:12,046 --> 02:09:13,485
Ulugan, yes.

1417
02:09:14,366 --> 02:09:16,565
Ulugan, who brings the apocalypse.

1418
02:09:20,286 --> 02:09:25,685
My glorious, fearless, merciless nokers.

1419
02:09:26,046 --> 02:09:31,805
Come here! Come and witness how Osman dies!

1420
02:09:42,486 --> 02:09:47,965
I will bury you along with
your glory in history, Osman.

1421
02:09:48,166 --> 02:09:50,125
I will destroy you.

1422
02:09:50,206 --> 02:09:52,805
This is the Anatolian plateau of Turks.

1423
02:09:52,806 --> 02:09:55,445
Here, history is written with blood.

1424
02:09:56,286 --> 02:09:59,525
We write history...

1425
02:10:00,406 --> 02:10:02,045
...and we change it.

1426
02:10:02,486 --> 02:10:06,885
Your words are stronger than your sword, Osman.

1427
02:10:07,966 --> 02:10:10,885
You're talking like this by relying on what?

1428
02:10:11,286 --> 02:10:12,765
You're desperate.

1429
02:10:12,926 --> 02:10:14,365
You're going to die.

1430
02:10:14,526 --> 02:10:19,565
I rely on the help of the desperate
and the hope of the hopeless!

1431
02:10:20,646 --> 02:10:22,285
And you?

1432
02:10:23,366 --> 02:10:25,325
You rely on your army?

1433
02:10:25,606 --> 02:10:29,005
Come on fight us. Let's see if you can.

1434
02:10:29,966 --> 02:10:30,925
I won't..

1435
02:10:30,926 --> 02:10:31,605
I won t.

1436
02:10:32,926 --> 02:10:36,645
...give you the honor of dying with my sword.

1437
02:10:36,926 --> 02:10:41,285
My nokers are going to kill you. Nokers, attack!

1438
02:11:17,166 --> 02:11:23,045
Well... We write history, we break history.

1439
02:11:23,486 --> 02:11:27,565
Especially when we say takbir from our hearts!

1440
02:11:28,086 --> 02:11:29,405
Allah is the greatest!

1441
02:11:29,486 --> 02:11:36,005
Allah is the greatest! Allah is the greatest!

1442
02:11:49,966 --> 02:11:52,285
I've been waiting for a long time...

1443
02:11:52,366 --> 02:11:57,925
...to say a mouthful takbir
in a tough fight like this!

1444
02:11:58,126 --> 02:12:02,285
Come on, brothers! Time to yell! 
Allah is the greatest!

1445
02:12:02,326 --> 02:12:08,925
Allah is the greatest! Allah is the greatest!

1446
02:12:11,126 --> 02:12:13,125
How is that possible?

1447
02:12:13,446 --> 02:12:16,685
-Where is my army?
-Deep in hell!

1448
02:12:40,326 --> 02:12:43,605
Keep coming here.

1449
02:12:57,166 --> 02:12:59,885
Even if they betray and let us down...

1450
02:13:00,326 --> 02:13:03,165
...we will never stop against heathens.

1451
02:13:03,526 --> 02:13:08,365
Now it's time to destroy nokers. Boran.

1452
02:13:09,166 --> 02:13:12,285
Alps, release the flying flames.

1453
02:13:58,726 --> 02:14:00,845
Smart move, Osman Bey.

1454
02:14:01,926 --> 02:14:05,365
Nokers got ruined. Now we are equal in numbers.

1455
02:14:05,566 --> 02:14:08,725
My alps and I will be with you, always.
-Ayaz Bey.

1456
02:14:09,206 --> 02:14:11,485
Slaughter the nokers coming in the back.

1457
02:14:11,646 --> 02:14:13,445
I will go face Ulugan.

1458
02:14:13,566 --> 02:14:17,125
Then wear their clothes and come after me.

1459
02:14:17,166 --> 02:14:19,165
As you order, my Bey.

1460
02:14:19,486 --> 02:14:23,125
Allah is the greatest!

1461
02:14:30,126 --> 02:14:31,925
Come on, alps.

1462
02:14:33,406 --> 02:14:37,405
You tried to play games
and tricks against me, huh?

1463
02:14:39,286 --> 02:14:41,725
My game ends with blood, though.

1464
02:14:42,166 --> 02:14:44,245
Betrayer.

1465
02:14:47,966 --> 02:14:51,165
We would never leave the
fate of Turks in your hands!

1466
02:14:51,766 --> 02:14:57,165
If there is no peace for us in these lands
there will be no peace for you either.

1467
02:14:57,926 --> 02:15:01,245
You will pay for killing my nokers.

1468
02:15:01,926 --> 02:15:03,525
Remember.

1469
02:15:03,926 --> 02:15:06,005
I'm still the superior one.

1470
02:15:06,286 --> 02:15:10,365
Here are the battlefield and Osman Bey.

1471
02:15:11,486 --> 02:15:15,525
You are too many but we are Turks.

1472
02:15:16,446 --> 02:15:20,725
The bigger they come, the harder they fall.

1473
02:15:27,446 --> 02:15:29,325
Now you're going to die.